cept: airside transit through Tijuana airport the Cross Border Xpress bridge from the airport linking terminals across the Mexican-US border the federal toll road 1D and Via Rápida through Tijuana to the border FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tecate in Baja California, including roads between Tijuana and Tecate."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Chihuahua, except: the city of Chihuahua the border crossing in Ciudad Juárez (accessed by federal toll road 45) federal toll road 45D connecting the cities of Chihuahua and Ciudad Juárez the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Chihuahua and towns immediately on this route including Creel the road from Creel via San Juanito to San Pedro state highway 16 from San Pedro to Chihuahua There are high levels of organised crime activity, particularly human and drugs trafficking."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Sinaloa, except: the cities of Los Mochis and Mazatlán road 32 that runs between El Fuerte and Los Mochis the 15D federal toll road that runs the length of the state the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Los Mochis, El Fuerte and the towns immediately on this route Armed robbery and vehicle theft has happened in El Fuerte."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Tamaulipas, except: the border crossing at Nuevo Laredo accessed from Monterrey by federal toll road 85D – you should travel during daylight hours federal highways 80, 81 and 85 between Tampico, Ciudad de Victoria and Magueyes, and the entire area of Tamaulipas south of these highways Tamaulipas is dangerous due to the presence of many organised crime groups who fight for control of drug trafficking routes."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Zacatecas."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south-west of the road 45D."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Michoacán, except the: city of Morelia accessed by federal toll roads 15D, 126 and 43; and the federal toll road 48D between the city of Morelia and the General Francisco Mujica airport town of Pátzcuaro accessed by federal toll roads 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips out to islands on Lake Pátzcuaro federal highway 15D Michoacán is one of Mexico’s most violent states with high levels of organised crime and very little security presence."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the border state of Colima, specifically the municipalities of: Acatlán de Juárez Amacueca Ameca Atemajac de Brizuela Atengo Atenguillo Atoyac Autlán de Navarro Ayutla Casimiro Castillo Chiquilistlán Cocula Cuautitlán de García Barragán Cuautla Ejutla El Grullo El Limón Gómez Farias Guachinango Juchitlán Mixtlán San Gabriel San Marcos San Martín Hidalgo Sayula Tapalpa Techaluta de Montenegro Tecolotlán Tenamaxtlán Teocuitatlán de Corona Tolimán Tonaya Tuxcacuesco Tuxcueca Unión de Tula Villa Corona Villa Purificación Zacoalco de Torres Zapotitlán de Vadill Zapotlán el Grande FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the northern municipalities of: Bolaños Chimaltitán Colotlán Hostotipaquillo Huejúcar Huequilla el Alto Mezquitic San Martin de Bolaños Santa Maria de los Ángeles Totatiche Villa Guerrero This is due to inaccessibility for security forces, lack of state control, drugs cultivation and high levels of violence between rival criminal groups."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the whole state of Colima, except the city of Manzanillo accessed by sea or by air via Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport, and direct travel via road 200 from the airport to Manzanillo."}],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mexico","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-07-16T16:08:09+01:00"}},"timing":{"peak":"Dec-Mar (calmest seas, clearest skies, 200ft+ viz; Dec24-Jan1 crowded/expensive spike)","shoulder":"Nov (~25-40% off Dec) and May (~20-30% off April); near-peak conditions","green":"May-Sep warmest water ~27-28C / calmest seas; summer humidity + hurricane risk Jun-Nov (peak Aug-Oct)","booking_window_lead_time":"peak dive weeks book well ahead; Chinchorro multi-day + private crewed dive-yacht = book months ahead (limited weather windows / small vessels)","out_of_season_fill_the_beds":"green-summer value story: warmest/calmest water + 20-40% off rooms, thinner crowds, pair with hurricane trip insurance","holiday_event_peaks":["Cozumel Carnival 2026: main parades Feb 14/15/17 (Fat Tue), run Feb 11-18, pre-Carnival Jan 17-Feb 8; floats with pre-Lenten lunar calendar","cruise-ship day-crowds congest San Miguel + nearer reefs — push early boats / south-zone sites"],"campaign_start_trigger":"open peak-season campaign Aug-Sep for Dec-Mar; shoulder push Sep-Oct (Nov) and Feb-Mar (May); Carnival micro-campaign Nov-Dec for mid-Feb"},"jewels":[{"name":"Palancar Reef (Gardens/Caves/Bricks/Horseshoe)","si_tag":"Dive Globally","status":"future","bookable":"2-tank day-boat dive","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.torntackies.com/cozumel-dive-sites/","hook":"iconic coral pinnacles, archways, swim-throughs, 100-ft+ viz, accessible drift","si":"diveglobal","blurb":"iconic coral pinnacles, archways, swim-throughs, 100-ft+ viz, accessible drift","commission":"dive-op DMC + Viator affiliate"},{"name":"Santa Rosa Wall","si_tag":"Dive Globally","status":"future","bookable":"advanced day-boat dive (expert-only)","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.torntackies.com/cozumel-dive-sites/","timing":"Dec-Mar","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"starts ~15 m / 45 ft and drops into the deep; expert-level, with eagle rays, turtles, nurse sharks and giant morays","si":"diveglobal","blurb":"starts ~15 m / 45 ft and drops into the deep; expert-level, with eagle rays, turtles, nurse sharks and giant morays","when":"Dec-Mar","commission":"dive-op DMC"},{"name":"Columbia Deep","si_tag":"Dive Globally","status":"future","bookable":"advanced day-boat dive","tier":"comfort","source":"https://cozumelscuba.com/cozumel-dive-sites/","timing":"Dec-Mar","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"diveglobal","when":"Dec-Mar","commission":"dive-op DMC"},{"name":"Banco Chinchorro atoll","si_tag":"Dive Liveaboards","status":"future","bookable":"multi-day/liveaboard-style from Xcalak/Mahahual","tier":"premier","source":"http://www.pelagiclife.org/chinchorro","timing":"Dec-Mar","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"liveaboard","when":"Dec-Mar","commission":"Aggressor/liveaboard reseller = Commissioned Agent on application"},{"name":"Palancar snorkel + El Cielo sandbar","si_tag":"Ocean Adventures","status":"future","bookable":"catamaran/snorkel tour","tier":"essential","source":"https://cozumelscuba.com/cozumel-dive-sites/","hook":"reef snorkel and shallow turquoise sandbar, no-fly-free family option","si":"ocean","blurb":"reef snorkel and shallow turquoise sandbar, no-fly-free family option","commission":"Viator/GYG affiliate + DMC"}],"faq":[{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for in Cozumel?","a":"Decompression discipline, not crime — this is a repetitive multi-day dive island. Follow DAN''s no-fly windows strictly (12h single, 18h multi-day, 24h conservative), because Cozumel''s day-boat profiles stack dives fast; the island has multiple chambers, but a bad no-fly call is the classic mistake. Also plan for dengue (repellent), bottled water and hurricane season (Jun–Nov).","source":"dan.org / travel.state.gov, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Is drift diving in Cozumel dangerous?","a":"No, when you take the drift briefing seriously — but it is not passive. Expect a near-constant ~1.5-knot current that does the swimming for you; do a controlled descent, stay with the group and dive master, deploy an SMB, and dive within your certification. Santa Rosa Wall is expert-only; Palancar Gardens suits most certified divers.","source":"cozumelscuba.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What are the best dive sites in Cozumel, and can beginners dive them?","a":"Palancar Gardens is the everyone-friendly classic — coral pinnacles, archways and swim-throughs at 100-ft-plus visibility with mild current — while Santa Rosa Wall and Columbia Deep are advanced drifts. Beginners and newly certified divers do best at Palancar; Santa Rosa, dropping from ~15 m into the blue, is expert-only.","source":"torntackies.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"diveglobal"},{"q":"Can I do a liveaboard from Cozumel?","a":"Not from Cozumel itself — it is a day-boat island. True liveaboard-style multi-day diving goes to Banco Chinchorro, ~30–35 nm off Costa Maya, launched from Xcalak or Mahahual to the south, not Cozumel. The luxury alternative near Cozumel is a private crewed dive-yacht charter, since overnight liveaboards are effectively banned inside the national park.","source":"pelagiclife.org / islandlifemexico.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"liveaboard"},{"q":"Can non-divers snorkel Cozumel, and what''s the reef fee?","a":"Yes — the reef is superb for snorkelers, from Palancar shallows to the El Cielo starfish sandbar by catamaran. Everyone entering the marine park pays the reef bracelet, MX$220 (~US$13) per person per day as of Jan 2026; snorkel tours carry no no-fly restriction, making them a good last-day option before a flight.","source":"cozumelmio.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"ocean"},{"q":"Is Cozumel good for a honeymoon or a couples'' dive trip?","a":"Yes — it pairs world-class diving with real staffed villas. Luxury Cozumel and Villa Experience run oceanfront staffed homes (chef, concierge) from ~US$450/night, and there is no branded ultra flag on-island, so for hotel-brand luxury couples ferry to Mayakoba (Rosewood, Banyan Tree) ~an hour away.","source":"luxurycozumel.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"When is the best time to dive Cozumel?","a":"December–March is peak, with the calmest seas, clearest skies and legendary 200-ft-plus visibility. November and May are the value sweet spots — near-peak conditions at ~25–40% (Nov) and ~20–30% (May) below Dec rates; May–September brings the warmest, calmest water (~27–28°C) but summer humidity and hurricane risk.","source":"sunsetcozumel.com / mexicotravelandleisure.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"planning"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Cozumel Diving: Drift the Mesoamerican Reef","meta_description":"Cozumel is the Caribbean''s drift-diving crown - Palancar, Santa Rosa Wall and the Mesoamerican Reef, with chambers, no-fly rules and the Chinchorro liveaboard hook.","slug":"cozumel-mexico","primary_keyword":"Cozumel drift diving","long_tail":["Cozumel dive sites Palancar Santa Rosa","Cozumel marine park fee 2026","Banco Chinchorro liveaboard","Cozumel recompression chamber","Mesoamerican Barrier Reef diving"],"search_language":["en","es-MX"],"local_keywords":["buceo en Cozumel","arrecife Palancar Santa Rosa","camara hiperbarica Cozumel","buceo de deriva Cozumel","Parque Nacional Arrecifes de Cozumel","Banco Chinchorro buceo","villa privada de lujo Cozumel"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","content_freshness":"2026-07-04"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"diveglobal","status":"future"},{"si":"liveaboard","status":"future","note":"Cozumel = day-boat reef diving; liveaboard/multi-day runs to Banco Chinchorro launch from Xcalak/Mahahual, NOT Cozumel"},{"si":"ocean","status":"future"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Private Paradise Villa","location":"Cozumel (on-island)","what":"oceanfront exclusive-use villa, sleeps up to 24, 40+ staff incl. 7 rotating chefs + British-butler-trained butlers","why_ultra":"full-buyout fully-staffed private-resort — the on-island ultra expression","earning":"villa-agency/DMC commission on application (agent-of-record; no net-rate resale)","virtuoso_value_add":"n/a standalone; attach Virtuoso mainland stay for perks","mor_posture":"clean agent-side; red-flag any villa-inventory mark-up","price_tier":"ultra","source":"https://privateparadisevilla.com/"},{"name":"Private crewed dive-yacht charter","location":"Cozumel / Riviera Maya (on-water)","what":"fully-crewed private yacht (captain+deckhand+dive master, chef/hostess on premium boats), 15+ sites + El Cielo, premium open bar","why_ultra":"ultra dive expression; only luxury ''liveaboard-style'' the park''s vessel-size rules allow (overnight liveaboards effectively banned in-park)","earning":"charter/DMC commission on application","virtuoso_value_add":"n/a direct; pair with Virtuoso stay","mor_posture":"agent-of-record on charter; no net-rate resale","price_tier":"ultra","source":"https://dayyachtcharters.com/cozumel-yacht-charters-luxury-boat-rentals.html"},{"name":"Riviera Maya branded ultra (Rosewood/Banyan Tree Mayakoba, Chable Maroma, Maroma Belmond)","location":"Riviera Maya mainland (ferry + short transfer)","what":"Forbes/branded ultra-luxury resorts + villas; private pools, top spas, PGA course","why_ultra":"nearest true branded ultra flag — no ultra flag on Cozumel itself","earning":"Virtuoso preferred rate + commission (or via host-Virtuoso)","virtuoso_value_add":"upgrade, daily breakfast for two, early check-in/late check-out, ~US$100 credit, VIP welcome (Mayakoba flags)","mor_posture":"standard Virtuoso agent-of-record","price_tier":"ultra","source":"https://www.rosewoodhotels.com/en/mayakoba-riviera-maya"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-04","hero":{"query":"Cozumel, Mexico"},"geo":{"lat":20.423,"lng":-86.9223}}'::jsonb, 30),
