:"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Cuenca''s signature: three great domes tiled in blue-and-white glaze from old Czechoslovakia, Romanesque-Revival, built 1885 over nearly a century","si":"culture","blurb":"Cuenca''s signature: three great domes tiled in blue-and-white glaze from old Czechoslovakia, Romanesque-Revival, built 1885 over nearly a century","when":"June–September  + secondary dry spell ~December","commission":"DMC city walking tour / activity affiliate"},{"name":"El Barranco + Río Tomebamba","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://trans-americas.com/city-travel-guide-cuenca-ecuador/","timing":"June–September  + secondary dry spell ~December","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"The terraced river-edge where colonial houses spill down to the water, walking paths, cafés and the old-town/modern-city dividing line. Free to wander","si":"culture","blurb":"The terraced river-edge where colonial houses spill down to the water, walking paths, cafés and the old-town/modern-city dividing line. Free to wander","when":"June–September  + secondary dry spell ~December","commission":"DMC walking tour; boutique-hotel proximity"},{"name":"Homero Ortega Panama-hat workshop & museum","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/homero-ortega-workshop-and-museum","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"The living home of the sombrero de paja toquilla — a family museum + active toquilla-straw workshop + boutique","si":"culture","blurb":"The living home of the sombrero de paja toquilla — a family museum + active toquilla-straw workshop + boutique","when":"year-round","commission":"DMC craft tour + boutique retail"},{"name":"Ingapirca — largest Inca ruin (Temple of the Sun)","si_tag":"culture","tier":"comfort","source":"https://happygringo.com/blog/ingapirca-ruins-ecuador/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"A rare Inca-Cañari blend crowned by the elliptical Temple of the Sun — the only one of its kind in the empire","si":"culture","blurb":"A rare Inca-Cañari blend crowned by the elliptical Temple of the Sun — the only one of its kind in the empire","when":"year-round","commission":"DMC full-day guided or self-serve bus + site entry"},{"name":"Gualaceo & Chordeleg craft villages (silver filigree + ikat)","si_tag":"culture","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.cuencabestours.com/day-tours/gualaceo-and-chordeleg-craft-making-villages-tour","timing":"June–September  + secondary dry spell ~December","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","when":"June–September  + secondary dry spell ~December","commission":"DMC craft-circuit day tour + artisan retail"},{"name":"Museo Pumapungo","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pumapungo_Museum","timing":"June–September  + secondary dry spell ~December","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Cuenca''s biggest museum — ethnographic + art collections and the Inca-era Pumapungo archaeological site/etno-botanical park on a hillock over the Tomebamba","si":"culture","blurb":"Cuenca''s biggest museum — ethnographic + art collections and the Inca-era Pumapungo archaeological site/etno-botanical park on a hillock over the Tomebamba","when":"June–September  + secondary dry spell ~December","commission":"DMC guided city/culture tour (entry free)"},{"name":"Mirador de Turi","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.lonelyplanet.com/ecuador/the-southern-highlands/cuenca/attractions/mirador-de-turi/a/poi-sig/436630/363371","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"The hilltop viewpoint over Cuenca''s colonial skyline — a chapel, restaurants and the classic photo, especially at sunset and during the Nov–Dec Christmas-lights season","si":"culture","blurb":"The hilltop viewpoint over Cuenca''s colonial skyline — a chapel, restaurants and the classic photo, especially at sunset and during the Nov–Dec Christmas-lights season","when":"year-round","commission":"DMC city tour; taxi/transfer"},{"name":"Cuenca festivals — Independence (Nov 3) & Pase del Niño (Dec 24)","si_tag":"culture","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.patrimoniocultural.gob.ec/pase-del-nino-viajero/","timing":"June–September  + secondary dry spell ~December","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"A three-day civic festival and Azuay''s largest religious parade — the two dates that most enrich a heritage-focused trip","si":"culture","blurb":"A three-day civic festival and Azuay''s largest religious parade — the two dates that most enrich a heritage-focused trip","when":"June–September  + secondary dry spell ~December","commission":"festival-timed lodging + DMC cultural programming"},{"name":"El Cajas National Park — Toreadora & páramo lakes (~3,960 m)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.moontravelguides.com/travel/outdoors/ecuadors-el-cajas-national-park/","timing":"June–September  + secondary dry spell ~December","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"28,000 ha, 786 lakes, wildflower páramo and rare polylepis stands","si":"expedition","blurb":"28,000 ha, 786 lakes, wildflower páramo and rare polylepis stands","when":"June–September  + secondary dry spell ~December","commission":"DMC/local guided hike or activity affiliate; park entry pass-through"},{"name":"Baños de Cuenca thermal circuit — Piedra de Agua","si_tag":"RHN / Wellness","tier":"essential","source":"https://travelwritingpro.com/piedra-de-agua-hot-springs-spa-banos-de-cuenca-ecuador/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"Volcanic hot springs 20 min from downtown, water surfacing at ~75°C and cooled to a bathing 36–40°C","si":"RHN / Wellness","blurb":"Volcanic hot springs 20 min from downtown, water surfacing at ~75°C and cooled to a bathing 36–40°C","when":"year-round","commission":"DMC add-on / spa entry pass-through + transfer"}],"faq":[{"q":"What makes Cuenca a UNESCO World Heritage city?","a":"Its historic center is a living colonial grid crowned by the New Cathedral — the Catedral de la Inmaculada Concepción, whose three blue-and-white domes were tiled with glaze from old Czechoslovakia and whose towers were left truncated by a load-bearing miscalculation. Built from 1885 over nearly a century, it is free to enter, with dome access monetized.","source":"en.wikipedia.org, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culture-&-heritage-—-future-si"},{"q":"Is Ingapirca worth the day trip from Cuenca?","a":"Yes — it is Ecuador''s largest Inca ruin, ~80 km north (~3,150 m), a rare Inca-Cañari blend crowned by the elliptical Temple of the Sun, the only one of its kind in the empire, built atop a Cañari sacred rock. Go guided full-day (highest margin) or self-serve by Transportes Cañar bus (~$3.50).","source":"happygringo.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culture-&-heritage-—-future-si"},{"q":"Is Cuenca a good romantic honeymoon base?","a":"Yes — it is a gentle, walkable heritage-city honeymoon, not a beach one. Restored 19th-century casonas like Mansión Alcázar (three blocks from Parque Calderón, with garden, spa and fine dining) and Hotel Santa Lucía anchor the boutique-colonial base, with the Baños de Cuenca thermal circuit — water surfacing at ~75°C — 20 minutes out.","source":"travelwritingpro.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"Can you hike El Cajas from Cuenca on your own?","a":"Only partly — go guided beyond the marked loops. El Cajas (28,000 ha, 786 lakes) has no cell signal and weather that turns in minutes; only the Laguna Toreadora and Laguna Llaviucu loops are well marked, and exposure deaths have occurred on unmarked trails. The ~2-hour Toreadora loop (~3,960 m) is self-guided-feasible for the acclimatized.","source":"moontravelguides.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for in Cuenca?","a":"Altitude, not crime. Cuenca sits at ~2,560 m, just above the 2,500 m AMS threshold — effects are usually mild and pass in 2–3 days — but El Cajas hiking at ~3,960–4,000 m is genuine high-altitude exertion. Take a slow first day, hydrate 3+ L/day, skip alcohol early, and do Cajas after a day or two in the city rather than on arrival.","source":"mytrip2ecuador.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Is El Cajas dangerous?","a":"It can be if you go off-trail unprepared — exposure deaths have occurred there. The park has no cell signal and weather changes in minutes; only the Toreadora and Llaviucu loops are well marked. Guided is strongly preferred beyond those two loops; carry layers, a rain shell, water and food regardless of forecast, and hike after acclimatizing.","source":"moontravelguides.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Cuenca & the Southern Andes, Ecuador — Travel Guide, El Cajas, Ingapirca & Panama Hats | TravelWell.World","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","freshness":"2026-07-07","search_language":"es-EC","local_keywords":["qué hacer en Cuenca Ecuador","Parque Nacional Cajas","Ingapirca","ruinas de Ingapirca desde Cuenca","sombrero de paja toquilla Cuenca","Gualaceo Chordeleg artesanías","Catedral Nueva de Cuenca cúpulas azules","Baños de Cuenca aguas termales","Pase del Niño Viajero","Independencia de Cuenca 3 de noviembre"],"hreflang":["en","es-EC"],"primary_keyword":"Cuenca & the Southern Andes"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"culture","status":"live"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Mansión Alcázar","location":"Cuenca historic center","earning":"Fora/Virtuoso where preferred; agency AoR + amenities","mor":"agency/hotel","tier":"$$$–$$$$"},{"name":"Hotel Santa Lucía","location":"Cuenca Old Town","earning":"agency AoR; Fora/Virtuoso if preferred","mor":"agency/hotel","tier":"$$$"},{"name":"Casa del Águila","location":"Cuenca","earning":"agency AoR; affiliate","mor":"agency/hotel","tier":"$$$"},{"name":"Hacienda stays (Azuay/Cañar countryside)","location":"outside Cuenca toward craft villages/Ingapirca","earning":"MoR / agency","mor":"agency/MoR","tier":"$$$"}],"source_verified":null,"hero":{"query":"Cuenca & the Southern Andes, Ecuador, Ecuador"},"geo":{"lat":-2.9005,"lng":-79.0045}}'::jsonb, 31),
  ('cusco-peru', '10S', 'Cusco & the Sacred Valley, Peru', 'Peru', 'Cusco & the Sacred Valley', 'live', 'verified', 'mountainValley', 'Cusco, Sacred Valley & Machu Picchu', '{"culture"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":null,"safety":{"emergency":"105","tourist_help":"iPerú WhatsApp 944 492 314","advisory_level":"L2","book_enabled":true,"bin":"freely bookable (L2)","consent_flow":false,"air_access_verified":true,"air_access":"Cusco (CUZ) via Lima (LIM)","altitude_m":{"cusco":3400,"rainbow_mountain_vinicunca":5200,"humantay_lake":4200,"salkantay_pass":4650},"altitude_rule":"Acclimatize 1–2 days in Cusco/valley before any high hike; gradual ascent; coca/soroche management; consider Diamox","water":"bottled/purified only","fcdo":{"posture":"AREA-RESTRICTED","quotes":[{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel Within 20km south of the Peru-Colombia border FCDO advises against all but essential travel to areas within 20km south of the Putumayo River and the border between Peru and Colombia (Loreto region) except for: the Amazon River the area of the triple border with Brazil and Colombia from and including the towns of Caballococha in Peru up to the actual triple border at Santa Rosa de Yavari town Valley of the Apurímac, Ene, and Mantaro Rivers ( VRAEM ) FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the Valley of the Apurímac, Ene, and Mantaro Rivers, also known as the VRAEM region."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advise against all but essential travel to these two areas for safety and security reasons."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to areas within 20km south of the Putumayo River and the border between Peru and Colombia (Loreto region) except for: the Amazon River the area of the triple border with Brazil and Colombia from and including the towns of Caballococha in Peru up to the actual triple border at Santa Rosa de Yavari town This is due to a high level of violence from organised criminal gangs who produce and traffic illegal drugs."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the Valley of the Apurímac, Ene and Mantaro Rivers, also known as the VRAEM region."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel."}],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/peru","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-06-22T23:35:12+01:00"}},"timing":{"peak":"May–August (Jun–Aug crowd apex)","event_peak":"Inti Raymi — June 24","inflection_curve_start":"early April","fire_date":"late March (Feb–Mar for Inti Raymi / Jun–Aug)","green_offseason":"November–March","binding_constraint":"capacity (Machu Picchu entry, trains, Inti Raymi lodging), not price"},"jewels":[{"name":"Rainbow Mountain (Vinicunca ~5,200 m)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","source":"https://altitude-peru.com/blog/vinicunca-altitude/","timing":"May–August","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the mineral-striped ridge that made the region viral. Extreme altitude; go guided and only after acclimatizing","si":"expedition","blurb":"the mineral-striped ridge that made the region viral. Extreme altitude; go guided and only after acclimatizing","when":"May–August","commission":"DMC private-guided / activity affiliate"},{"name":"Palccoyo (gentler rainbow)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","source":"https://localtrekkersperu.com/blog/rainbow-mountain-peru-vinicunca-guide/","timing":"May–August","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"three colored ridges reached by a short, far-less-punishing walk; the smart pick for travelers who want the palette without the 5,200 m gut-check","si":"expedition","blurb":"three colored ridges reached by a short, far-less-punishing walk; the smart pick for travelers who want the palette without the 5,200 m gut-check","when":"May–August","commission":"DMC / activity affiliate"},{"name":"Humantay Lake (~4,200 m)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.salkantaytrekking.com/traditional/cusco/humantay-lake-full-day/","hook":"a turquoise glacial lake under Salkantay''s snows; a demanding half-day climb from Soraypampa","si":"expedition","blurb":"a turquoise glacial lake under Salkantay''s snows; a demanding half-day climb from Soraypampa","commission":"DMC / activity affiliate"},{"name":"Salkantay Pass trek (~4,650 m)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"premier","source":"https://www.salkantaytrekking.com/trekking-in-peru/cusco/salkantay-rainbow-mountain-trek-7d/","timing":"May–August","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the high alternative to the Inca Trail, often chained to Machu Picchu; multi-day, guided","si":"expedition","blurb":"the high alternative to the Inca Trail, often chained to Machu Picchu; multi-day, guided","when":"May–August","commission":"DMC multi-day trek"},{"name":"San Blas artisan barrio, Cusco","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.salkantaytrekking.com/blog/maras-and-moray-sacred-valley-guide/","timing":"May–August","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the steep bohemian quarter of workshops, silversmiths and cafés above the Plaza. Free to wander; monetizes through walking tours + boutique retail","si":"culture","blurb":"the steep bohemian quarter of workshops, silversmiths and cafés above the Plaza. Free to wander; monetizes through walking tours + boutique retail","when":"May–August","commission":"DMC city tour / affiliate"},{"name":"Sacsayhuamán + Q''enqo","si_tag":"culture","tier":"comfort","source":"https://turismoliberty.pe/en/cusco-tourist-ticket-2026/","timing":"May–August","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the cyclopean fortress-temple above Cusco and the nearby carved ritual site; both on the Boleto Turístico Circuit I","si":"culture","blurb":"the cyclopean fortress-temple above Cusco and the nearby carved ritual site; both on the Boleto Turístico Circuit I","when":"May–August","commission":"DMC guided; Boleto Turístico entry"},{"name":"Pisac market + ruins","si_tag":"culture","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.salkantaytrekking.com/blog/maras-and-moray-sacred-valley-guide/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"the classic Andean textile/craft market beneath dramatic terraced ruins and an ancient cliff cemetery","si":"culture","blurb":"the classic Andean textile/craft market beneath dramatic terraced ruins and an ancient cliff cemetery","when":"year-round","commission":"DMC circuit; Boleto Turístico III"},{"name":"Ollantaytambo living-Inca town","si_tag":"culture","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.machupicchureservations.org/tour/sacred-valley-tour-full-day-2/","timing":"May–August","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"one of the last inhabited Inca settlements, streets still fed by working 500-year-old canals","si":"culture","blurb":"one of the last inhabited Inca settlements, streets still fed by working 500-year-old canals","when":"May–August","commission":"DMC circuit + rail; Boleto Turístico III"},{"name":"Maras salt pans + Moray terraces","si_tag":"culture","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.salkantaytrekking.com/blog/maras-and-moray-sacred-valley-guide/","timing":"May–August","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"4,500+ hand-worked salt pools fed by a pre-Inca spring, and the Inca''s circular \"agricultural laboratory\" of microclimate terraces. Iconic photography, deep story","si":"culture","blurb":"4,500+ hand-worked salt pools fed by a pre-Inca spring, and the Inca''s circular \"agricultural laboratory\" of microclimate terraces. Iconic photography, deep story","when":"May–August","commission":"DMC circuit; Boleto Turístico III (Moray)"},{"name":"Chinchero weaving village","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.salkantaytrekking.com/blog/maras-and-moray-sacred-valley-guide/","timing":"May–August","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the \"birthplace of the rainbow,\" high-plateau town with a Textile Interpretation Center where women demonstrate natural-dye alpaca weaving","si":"culture","blurb":"the \"birthplace of the rainbow,\" high-plateau town with a Textile Interpretation Center where women demonstrate natural-dye alpaca weaving","when":"May–August","commission":"DMC circuit + artisan retail; Boleto Turístico III"},{"name":"Cusco Cathedral + Qorikancha","si_tag":"culture","tier":"comfort","source":"https://turismoliberty.pe/en/cusco-tourist-ticket-2026/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"the colonial cathedral on the Plaza de Armas and the Inca Temple of the Sun whose gold-clad walls the Spanish built Santo Domingo atop","si":"culture","blurb":"the colonial cathedral on the Plaza de Armas and the Inca Temple of the Sun whose gold-clad walls the Spanish built Santo Domingo atop","when":"year-round","commission":"DMC city tour; separate admissions"},{"name":"San Pedro Market, Cusco","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.salkantaytrekking.com/blog/maras-and-moray-sacred-valley-guide/","timing":"May–August","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the working city market: produce, cheeses, juices, textiles, street food; the sensory anchor of a food-focused day","si":"culture","blurb":"the working city market: produce, cheeses, juices, textiles, street food; the sensory anchor of a food-focused day","when":"May–August","commission":"DMC food/market tour"},{"name":"Pisco + Andean cuisine chef''s-table","si_tag":"RHN / Culinary","tier":"premier","source":"https://luxurylatinamerica.com/blog/2024/12/10/stay-in-the-sacred-valley/","timing":"May–August","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the high-Andes ingredient story at chef''s-table and tasting-menu level, paired with pisco. Sacred Valley luxe lodges and Cusco''s fine-dining scene carry this","si":"RHN / Culinary","blurb":"the high-Andes ingredient story at chef''s-table and tasting-menu level, paired with pisco. Sacred Valley luxe lodges and Cusco''s fine-dining scene carry this","when":"May–August","commission":"DMC private dining / lodge F&B"}],"faq":[{"q":"Do you need to acclimatize before Rainbow Mountain?","a":"Yes — acclimatize 1–2 days minimum in Cusco or the valley before any high hike, and never climb Rainbow Mountain on your first or second day. It matters because more than a third of travelers to Cusco feel altitude sickness, the summit sits at ~5,200 m (roughly 11% effective oxygen), and the core risk is acute mountain sickness, not terrain. Go guided — reputable operators carry oxygen, manage pace and pull travelers who deteriorate.","source":"turismoliberty.pe, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"What does the Cusco Tourist Ticket cover?","a":"The integral Boleto Turístico costs S/130 (~$35), is valid 10 days across 16 sites, and is cash-only in soles with no online option. Note what it does not cover: Machu Picchu, Qorikancha, the Cathedral, Rainbow Mountain and Humantay all require separate admission, so budget those as pass-through costs on top.","source":"turismoliberty.pe, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"Which are the best luxury lodges in the Sacred Valley and Cusco?","a":"The honeymoon spine runs from Cusco''s Belmond Palacio Nazarenas (55 oxygen-enriched all-suites) and Belmond Monasterio (a 16th-century monastery, 117 rooms) out to the valley''s explora Valle Sagrado, Sol y Luna (Relais & Châteaux) and Tambo del Inka — the Luxury Collection resort with its own private rail station to Machu Picchu.","source":"belmond.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"When do you need to book for Inti Raymi and peak season?","a":"Book 3–4 months out — by late March, ideally February — for June–August and Inti Raymi trips, because capacity, not price, is what runs out. Inti Raymi (the Festival of the Sun) falls on June 24 and sells the city out months ahead, and Machu Picchu tickets, trains and hotels are capacity-capped in peak season.","source":"perurail.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"What''s the real risk in Cusco — is it altitude?","a":"Yes — altitude outranks crime by a wide margin. Cusco sits at ~3,400 m and Rainbow Mountain at ~5,200 m, and more than a third of travelers feel altitude sickness (soroche), some moderate-to-severe. Acclimatize 1–2 days before any high hike, ascend gradually, hydrate, use coca, and discuss prophylactic acetazolamide (Diamox) with a physician; the emergency number is 105.","source":"turismoliberty.pe, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Is Rainbow Mountain dangerous?","a":"The danger is altitude, not the walk. At ~5,200 m the core risk is acute mountain sickness, so guided is strongly preferred — reputable operators carry oxygen, manage pace and pull travelers who deteriorate — and the non-negotiable rule is to acclimatize 1–2 days first. Travelers who want the color without the 5,200 m gut-check can take Palccoyo, the gentler-altitude \"rainbow\" alternative.","source":"altitude-peru.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Cusco & the Sacred Valley, Peru — Travel Guide, Treks, Luxury Lodges & Altitude Tips | TravelWell.World","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","freshness":"2026-07-07","search_language":"es-PE","local_keywords":["qué hacer en Cusco","Valle Sagrado tour","Montaña de 7 Colores","boleto turístico Cusco 2026","mal de altura Cusco soroche","Laguna Humantay","Inti Raymi 24 de junio","Maras Moray salineras","Ollantaytambo qué ver"],"hreflang":["en","es-PE"],"primary_keyword":"Cusco & the Sacred Valley"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"culture","status":"live"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Belmond Palacio Nazarenas","location":"Cusco","earning":"Virtuoso preferred; agency AoR + VIP amenities","mor":"agency/hotel","tier":"$$$$"},{"name":"Belmond Monasterio","location":"Cusco","earning":"Virtuoso preferred; agency AoR","mor":"agency/hotel","tier":"$$$$"},{"name":"Belmond Río Sagrado","location":"Sacred Valley","earning":"Virtuoso/Belmond preferred; agency AoR","mor":"agency/hotel","tier":"$$$$"},{"name":"JW Marriott El Convento Cusco","location":"Cusco","earning":"Marriott Luxury/STARS; agency AoR + Bonvoy","mor":"agency/hotel","tier":"$$$$"},{"name":"Inkaterra La Casona","location":"Cusco","earning":"Relais & Châteaux/Virtuoso; agency AoR","mor":"agency/hotel","tier":"$$$$"},{"name":"explora Valle Sagrado","location":"Sacred Valley","earning":"Virtuoso; agency AoR","mor":"agency/hotel","tier":"$$$$"},{"name":"Sol y Luna","location":"Sacred Valley","earning":"Relais & Châteaux/Virtuoso; agency AoR","mor":"agency/hotel","tier":"$$$$"},{"name":"Tambo del Inka, a Luxury Collection Resort & Spa","location":"Sacred Valley (Urubamba)","earning":"Marriott Luxury/STARS; agency AoR + Bonvoy","mor":"agency/hotel","tier":"$$$$"}],"source_verified":null,"hero":{"query":"Cusco & the Sacred Valley, Peru, Peru"},"geo":{"lat":-13.5319,"lng":-71.9675}}'::jsonb, 32),
