but essential travel to the state of Colima, except the city of Manzanillo accessed by sea or air via the Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport, and direct travel via road 200 from the airport to Manzanillo."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Guerrero, except the town of Zihuatanejo/Ixtapa accessed by air."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to within 40km of the Guatemalan border between the Pacific Coast up to and including the border crossing at Gracias a Dio."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel on Federal Highway 199 (Carretera Federal 199) between Rancho Nuevo (just outside San Cristobal de las Casas) and the Chancalá junction just outside Palenque (where Federal Highway 199 meets Federal Highway 307)."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the city of Acapulco."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tijuana, except: airside transit through Tijuana airport the Cross Border Xpress bridge from the airport linking terminals across the Mexican-US border the federal toll road 1D and Via Rápida through Tijuana to the border FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tecate in Baja California, including roads between Tijuana and Tecate."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Chihuahua, except: the city of Chihuahua the border crossing in Ciudad Juárez (accessed by federal toll road 45) federal toll road 45D connecting the cities of Chihuahua and Ciudad Juárez the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Chihuahua and towns immediately on this route including Creel the road from Creel via San Juanito to San Pedro state highway 16 from San Pedro to Chihuahua There are high levels of organised crime activity, particularly human and drugs trafficking."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Sinaloa, except: the cities of Los Mochis and Mazatlán road 32 that runs between El Fuerte and Los Mochis the 15D federal toll road that runs the length of the state the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Los Mochis, El Fuerte and the towns immediately on this route Armed robbery and vehicle theft has happened in El Fuerte."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Tamaulipas, except: the border crossing at Nuevo Laredo accessed from Monterrey by federal toll road 85D – you should travel during daylight hours federal highways 80, 81 and 85 between Tampico, Ciudad de Victoria and Magueyes, and the entire area of Tamaulipas south of these highways Tamaulipas is dangerous due to the presence of many organised crime groups who fight for control of drug trafficking routes."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Zacatecas."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south-west of the road 45D."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Michoacán, except the: city of Morelia accessed by federal toll roads 15D, 126 and 43; and the federal toll road 48D between the city of Morelia and the General Francisco Mujica airport town of Pátzcuaro accessed by federal toll roads 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips out to islands on Lake Pátzcuaro federal highway 15D Michoacán is one of Mexico’s most violent states with high levels of organised crime and very little security presence."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the border state of Colima, specifically the municipalities of: Acatlán de Juárez Amacueca Ameca Atemajac de Brizuela Atengo Atenguillo Atoyac Autlán de Navarro Ayutla Casimiro Castillo Chiquilistlán Cocula Cuautitlán de García Barragán Cuautla Ejutla El Grullo El Limón Gómez Farias Guachinango Juchitlán Mixtlán San Gabriel San Marcos San Martín Hidalgo Sayula Tapalpa Techaluta de Montenegro Tecolotlán Tenamaxtlán Teocuitatlán de Corona Tolimán Tonaya Tuxcacuesco Tuxcueca Unión de Tula Villa Corona Villa Purificación Zacoalco de Torres Zapotitlán de Vadill Zapotlán el Grande FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the northern municipalities of: Bolaños Chimaltitán Colotlán Hostotipaquillo Huejúcar Huequilla el Alto Mezquitic San Martin de Bolaños Santa Maria de los Ángeles Totatiche Villa Guerrero This is due to inaccessibility for security forces, lack of state control, drugs cultivation and high levels of violence between rival criminal groups."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the whole state of Colima, except the city of Manzanillo accessed by sea or by air via Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport, and direct travel via road 200 from the airport to Manzanillo."}],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mexico","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-07-16T16:08:09+01:00"}},"timing":{"peak":["Summer (Jun-Sep)","Fiestas de la Vendimia (late Jul - late Aug)"],"secondary_peak":"Gray-whale migration Dec-Apr (offshore, peak Jan-Mar)","inflection":["Late spring (May-early Jun)","Autumn shoulder (Oct)"],"fire_date":"curve-start minus 1-2 weeks (fire Vendimia ~early Jul; whale season ~early Dec)","baseline":"cruise-day pulse year-round"},"jewels":[{"name":"La Bufadora blowhole + Punta Banda","si_tag":"GEA/Coastal","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.bajabound.com/destinations/ensenada/labufadora","timing":"[''Summer '', ''Fiestas de la Vendimia '']","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"GEA/Coastal","when":"[''Summer '', ''Fiestas de la Vendimia '']","commission":"GetYourGuide/Viator excursion + DMC transfer (blowhole free)"},{"name":"Gray-whale migration (offshore Dec-Apr)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.seakayakadventures.com/blog/top-10-things-you-need-know-about-baja-gray-whale-season","si":"expedition","commission":"licensed whale-watch charter + affiliate"},{"name":"Sportfishing - Todos Santos Bay","si_tag":"GEA/Coastal","tier":"comfort","source":"https://sergiosfishing.com/whales/","timing":"[''Summer '', ''Fiestas de la Vendimia '']","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"GEA/Coastal","when":"[''Summer '', ''Fiestas de la Vendimia '']","commission":"charter operator commission"},{"name":"Mercado Negro fish market + fish-taco birthplace","si_tag":"culinary","tier":"essential","source":"https://mexiconewsdaily.com/food/the-mystery-behind-the-invention-of-the-baja-fish-taco/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"culinary","when":"year-round","commission":"culinary/market tour affiliate + DMC"},{"name":"La Guerrerense (Sabina Bandera tostadas)","si_tag":"culinary","tier":"essential","source":"https://guide.michelin.com/us/en/baja-california/ensenada_2059847/restaurant/sabina","timing":"[''Summer '', ''Fiestas de la Vendimia '']","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culinary","when":"[''Summer '', ''Fiestas de la Vendimia '']","commission":"Sabina restaurant reservation + food-tour affiliate (cart non-commissionable)"},{"name":"Guadalupe/San Quintin oysters + aquaculture","si_tag":"culinary","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.bajacalifornia.travel/en/editorial/you-have-to-try-this-why-san-quintin-oysters-are-bajas-best-kept-secret","timing":"[''Summer '', ''Fiestas de la Vendimia '']","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culinary","when":"[''Summer '', ''Fiestas de la Vendimia '']","commission":"farm-tour experience operator + culinary DMC"},{"name":"Valle de Guadalupe wine day","si_tag":"Culinary/Romance","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.winetraveler.com/mexico/best-valle-de-guadalupe-wineries/","timing":"[''Summer '', ''Fiestas de la Vendimia '']","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Drink-and-drive is the 1 fire — unlit rural roads between wineries Driver/guide strongly recommended","si":"Culinary/Romance","blurb":"Drink-and-drive is the 1 fire — unlit rural roads between wineries Driver/guide strongly recommended","when":"[''Summer '', ''Fiestas de la Vendimia '']","commission":"wine-tour operator + winery reservations + hotel packages"},{"name":"Ensenada Malecon + Riviera del Pacifico Cultural Center","si_tag":"Romance/Culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hotel_Riviera_del_Pac%C3%ADfico","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"Romance/Culture","when":"year-round","commission":"city/culture tour affiliate (center entry low/free)"}],"faq":[{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for?","a":"Drink-and-drive on wine roads, and the cold Pacific — not the Mexicali cartel context, which lies far east and is never transited on the Ensenada corridor. Use a driver for any Valle de Guadalupe tasting day, treat the open Pacific as look-don''t-swim (strong riptides, cold water), and route serious trauma north to San Diego.","source":"travel.state.gov, 2026-05-29","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Where do I eat the famous fish tacos?","a":"Around the Mercado Negro, where they were arguably invented. Ensenada is credited as the birthplace of the modern Baja fish taco (c.1960), and doña Sabina Bandera''s La Guerrerense cart — a 2013 World Street Food Congress medalist and MICHELIN-recognized name — is the must-eat; nearby San Quintín Kumamoto oysters extend the culinary lane.","source":"mexiconewsdaily.com / guide.michelin.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culinary-—-future"},{"q":"What is La Bufadora and when''s it best?","a":"It''s one of North America''s largest marine geysers, best at high tide. On the Punta Banda peninsula, La Bufadora shoots seawater up to ~100 feet when swell compresses air in a sea cave; entry is free (nominal parking), and winter swells give the biggest spouts. Mind the slippery, unfenced cliff edges.","source":"bajabound.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Can I do Valle de Guadalupe as a day trip?","a":"Yes — it''s ~40 minutes northeast, with 250+ wineries and a farm-to-table scene. Book a guided wine day with a driver rather than self-driving, since the rural roads between wineries are the #1 safety fire; the Fiestas de la Vendimia (late Jul–late Aug) is the demand apex and sells out first.","source":"winetraveler.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"Can I see gray whales from Ensenada?","a":"Yes — offshore, December–April, peak January–March. Gray whales pass along the Pacific coast Ensenada→San Quintín on the longest mammal migration on earth; go with a licensed charter (life vests, weather-holds), noting the \"friendly\" lagoon nurseries lie farther south in Baja California Sur.","source":"seakayakadventures.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"expedition"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Ensenada, Mexico: La Bufadora, Fish Tacos & Valle de Guadalupe Wine Gateway | TravelWell","search_language":"es-MX","local_keywords":["qué hacer en Ensenada","La Bufadora","tacos de pescado Ensenada","tour Valle de Guadalupe desde Ensenada","La Guerrerense tostadas","Mercado Negro Ensenada","ballenas grises Ensenada"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister - commercial pilot, 56 countries","freshness":"2026-07-07"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":null,"ultra":[{"property":"Banyan Tree Veya Valle de Guadalupe","location":"Valle de Guadalupe (inland cross-ref)","fit":"brand-flag ultra; Amex FHR","mor":"consortia/FHR commission + amenities","tier":"$$$$$"},{"property":"Bruma Wine Resort","location":"Valle de Guadalupe (cross-ref)","fit":"high-design boutique-luxury","mor":"villa-rate/boutique consortia","tier":"$$$$"},{"property":"Encuentro Guadalupe","location":"Valle de Guadalupe (cross-ref)","fit":"design-forward pioneer","mor":"boutique consortia","tier":"$$$$"},{"property":"Hotel Punta Morro","location":"Ensenada coast","fit":"upper-boutique ceiling (in-town best)","mor":"direct/boutique commission","tier":"$$$"}],"source_verified":null,"hero":{"query":"Ensenada, Mexico, Mexico"},"geo":{"lat":31.8667,"lng":-116.5964}}'::jsonb, 35)
