ral Highway 15D State of Jalisco FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the border with the state of Colima."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the northern municipalities of: Bolaños Chimaltitán Colotlán Hostotipaquillo Huejúcar Huequilla el Alto Mezquitic San Martin de Bolaños Santa Maria de los Ángeles Totatiche Villa Guerrero State of Colima FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Colima, except the city of Manzanillo accessed by sea or air via the Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport, and direct travel via road 200 from the airport to Manzanillo."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Guerrero, except the town of Zihuatanejo/Ixtapa accessed by air."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to within 40km of the Guatemalan border between the Pacific Coast up to and including the border crossing at Gracias a Dio."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel on Federal Highway 199 (Carretera Federal 199) between Rancho Nuevo (just outside San Cristobal de las Casas) and the Chancalá junction just outside Palenque (where Federal Highway 199 meets Federal Highway 307)."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the city of Acapulco."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tijuana, except: airside transit through Tijuana airport the Cross Border Xpress bridge from the airport linking terminals across the Mexican-US border the federal toll road 1D and Via Rápida through Tijuana to the border FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tecate in Baja California, including roads between Tijuana and Tecate."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Chihuahua, except: the city of Chihuahua the border crossing in Ciudad Juárez (accessed by federal toll road 45) federal toll road 45D connecting the cities of Chihuahua and Ciudad Juárez the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Chihuahua and towns immediately on this route including Creel the road from Creel via San Juanito to San Pedro state highway 16 from San Pedro to Chihuahua There are high levels of organised crime activity, particularly human and drugs trafficking."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Sinaloa, except: the cities of Los Mochis and Mazatlán road 32 that runs between El Fuerte and Los Mochis the 15D federal toll road that runs the length of the state the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Los Mochis, El Fuerte and the towns immediately on this route Armed robbery and vehicle theft has happened in El Fuerte."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Tamaulipas, except: the border crossing at Nuevo Laredo accessed from Monterrey by federal toll road 85D – you should travel during daylight hours federal highways 80, 81 and 85 between Tampico, Ciudad de Victoria and Magueyes, and the entire area of Tamaulipas south of these highways Tamaulipas is dangerous due to the presence of many organised crime groups who fight for control of drug trafficking routes."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Zacatecas."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south-west of the road 45D."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Michoacán, except the: city of Morelia accessed by federal toll roads 15D, 126 and 43; and the federal toll road 48D between the city of Morelia and the General Francisco Mujica airport town of Pátzcuaro accessed by federal toll roads 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips out to islands on Lake Pátzcuaro federal highway 15D Michoacán is one of Mexico’s most violent states with high levels of organised crime and very little security presence."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the border state of Colima, specifically the municipalities of: Acatlán de Juárez Amacueca Ameca Atemajac de Brizuela Atengo Atenguillo Atoyac Autlán de Navarro Ayutla Casimiro Castillo Chiquilistlán Cocula Cuautitlán de García Barragán Cuautla Ejutla El Grullo El Limón Gómez Farias Guachinango Juchitlán Mixtlán San Gabriel San Marcos San Martín Hidalgo Sayula Tapalpa Techaluta de Montenegro Tecolotlán Tenamaxtlán Teocuitatlán de Corona Tolimán Tonaya Tuxcacuesco Tuxcueca Unión de Tula Villa Corona Villa Purificación Zacoalco de Torres Zapotitlán de Vadill Zapotlán el Grande FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the northern municipalities of: Bolaños Chimaltitán Colotlán Hostotipaquillo Huejúcar Huequilla el Alto Mezquitic San Martin de Bolaños Santa Maria de los Ángeles Totatiche Villa Guerrero This is due to inaccessibility for security forces, lack of state control, drugs cultivation and high levels of violence between rival criminal groups."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the whole state of Colima, except the city of Manzanillo accessed by sea or by air via Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport, and direct travel via road 200 from the airport to Manzanillo."}],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mexico","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-07-16T16:08:09+01:00"}},"timing":{"peak":"Nov-Apr (dry desert winter, calm seas); rides La Paz whale-shark high season Oct-Apr","shoulder":"May & Sep (warm water, sea lions open, softer demand)","green":"Jun-Aug (summer heat, hurricane window, sea-lion colony closed Jun 1-Aug 31 - beach/snorkel day-trips only)","booking_window_lead_time":"no island hotel; permitted camp beds tiny (Camp Cecil 8 tents, Nov-Apr, 2-night min) - book camps 3-6 months ahead; day tours days-weeks out, peak sea-lion days fill faster","out_of_season_fill_the_beds":"beach/snorkel day tours, San Rafaelito reef (sea-lion substitute during closure), kayak/SUP among cliffs, private sailing charters","holiday_event_peaks":"Christmas-New Year, Semana Santa, sea-lion core Sep-May; Camp Cecil Nov-Apr maps to peak","campaign_start_trigger":"camp/private-sailing campaigns May-Jul (Nov opening + limited beds); sea-lion day-tour campaigns Aug-Sep ahead of fall reopening; summer day-trip value in spring","flag":"sea lions closed Jun 1-Aug 31; summer overlaps hurricane season Jun-Nov; NO lodging except seasonal 8-tent camp","sources":["https://www.thoroughlytravel.com/isla-espiritu-santo/","https://scubaboard.com/community/threads/la-paz-sea-lion-colony-closed-for-snorkel-scuba-june-1-aug-31.621077/","https://www.islands.com/story/resorts/the-glamping-experience-of-isla-espiritu-santo-camp-cecil/"]},"jewels":[{"name":"Los Islotes sea-lion snorkel","si_tag":"Global Expedition Adventures","status":"live","tier":"comfort","bookable":"permitted day tour from La Paz (Sep-May)","source":"https://www.goworldtravel.com/snorkeling-sea-lions-sea-of-cortez/","hook":"swim with 600+ California sea lions at one of Mexico''s healthiest colonies","si":"expedition","blurb":"swim with 600+ California sea lions at one of Mexico''s healthiest colonies","commission":"local operator + Journey Mexico DMC + Viator affiliate"},{"name":"Full-day island snorkel + cove landing","si_tag":"Global Expedition Adventures","status":"live","tier":"premier","bookable":"permitted day tour incl. CONANP bracelet","source":"https://www.thoroughlytravel.com/isla-espiritu-santo/","hook":"pink-cliff coves, white-sand beaches, reef snorkel on an uninhabited UNESCO island","si":"expedition","blurb":"pink-cliff coves, white-sand beaches, reef snorkel on an uninhabited UNESCO island","commission":"local operator + DMC"},{"name":"Kayak / SUP among the cliffs","si_tag":"Global Expedition Adventures","status":"live","tier":"comfort","bookable":"kayak/SUP eco tour","source":"https://ecomigrations.com/tour/espiritu-santo-island-sea-lion-snorkeling-paddleboarding-tour/","hook":"paddle the empty coves and sea-lion waters; low-impact, all-ages","si":"expedition","blurb":"paddle the empty coves and sea-lion waters; low-impact, all-ages","commission":"eco operator (Eco Migrations) + GYG affiliate"},{"name":"Overnight glamping (Camp Cecil)","si_tag":"Global Expedition Adventures","status":"live","tier":"luxury","bookable":"TOSEA operator package (Nov-Apr, 2-night min, from ~$375 pp)","source":"https://www.islands.com/story/resorts/the-glamping-experience-of-isla-espiritu-santo-camp-cecil/","timing":"Nov-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"sleep on the island — 8 solar tents, sea lions off the beach, all-inclusive naturalist","si":"expedition","blurb":"sleep on the island — 8 solar tents, sea lions off the beach, all-inclusive naturalist","when":"Nov-Apr","commission":"TOSEA / host-Virtuoso on application"},{"name":"San Rafaelito reef snorkel/dive","si_tag":"Ocean Adventures / Dive Globally","status":"future","tier":"comfort","bookable":"dive/snorkel charter (sea-lion-closure substitute)","source":"https://scubaboard.com/community/threads/la-paz-sea-lion-colony-closed-for-snorkel-scuba-june-1-aug-31.621077/","hook":"the sea-lion-closure substitute reef; also a fine standalone snorkel","si":"Ocean Adventures / Dive Globally","blurb":"the sea-lion-closure substitute reef; also a fine standalone snorkel","commission":"dive operator + affiliate"}],"faq":[{"q":"When can I snorkel with sea lions at Los Islotes?","a":"September through May — the colony of 600+ California sea lions closes Jun 1–Aug 31 for pupping and mating, when operators substitute the San Rafaelito reef. It''s a snorkel-only, no-touch encounter with a licensed operator, usually on a ~$100–150 full-day island tour.","source":"goworldtravel.com / scubaboard.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Can I stay overnight on Espíritu Santo?","a":"Only at Camp Cecil, a permitted 8-tent solar camp open Nov–Apr (2-night minimum) — there are no hotels, roads or cell service on this protected, uninhabited UNESCO island. Everyone else visits sunrise-to-sunset by permitted boat and carries everything in and out.","source":"islands.com / thoroughlytravel.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"wildlife"},{"q":"How do I visit if the sea lions are closed?","a":"Come for the empty island itself — pink-cliff coves, white-sand beaches, kayak/SUP and the San Rafaelito reef snorkel that substitutes for Los Islotes in summer. Private crewed sailing charters (from ~$600+ per boat) are the calmest way to see it.","source":"thoroughlytravel.com / scubaboard.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"ocean"},{"q":"What''s the real risk on an uninhabited island?","a":"No services, no cell signal and no medical facilities. Any emergency requires a boat back to La Paz, then Hospital Salvatierra or private clinics with air-evac for major trauma — so carry travel medical + evacuation insurance and bring your own water, food and sun protection.","source":"hgejms.gob.mx / thoroughlytravel.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Espíritu Santo Island: UNESCO Sea-of-Cortez Guide","meta_description":"Snorkel with sea lions at Los Islotes and land on uninhabited, UNESCO-listed Espíritu Santo from La Paz — permits, seasons (colony closed Jun–Aug) and how to book.","slug":"espiritu-santo-island-mexico","primary_keyword":"Espíritu Santo island","long_tail":["Espiritu Santo tour from La Paz","Los Islotes sea lion snorkel season","Espiritu Santo CONANP permit","Camp Cecil glamping Espiritu Santo","uninhabited island Sea of Cortez"],"search_language":["en","es-MX"],"local_keywords":["Isla Espíritu Santo tour desde La Paz","nadar con lobos marinos Los Islotes","permiso CONANP Isla Espíritu Santo","Parque Nacional Archipiélago Espíritu Santo","campamento Camp Cecil Espíritu Santo","snorkel Mar de Cortés isla deshabitada"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","content_freshness":"2026-07-04"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"expedition","status":"live"},{"si":"Ocean Adventures / Dive Globally","status":"future"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Camp Cecil de la Isla","posture":"only overnight on the UNESCO island; eco-luxe 8-tent solar camp (TOSEA)","price_tier":"ultra","earning":"on application / host-Virtuoso or TOSEA operator terms","virtuoso_value_add":"private full-camp buy-out (8 tents) + naturalist upgrade on application","mor":"no net-rate resale","source":"https://www.islands.com/story/resorts/the-glamping-experience-of-isla-espiritu-santo-camp-cecil/"},{"name":"Private crewed sailing charter (Espiritu Santo)","posture":"ultra way to see the island without lodging (~$600+/boat and up)","price_tier":"ultra","earning":"on application via host / Journey Mexico DMC","virtuoso_value_add":"private naturalist + provisioning on application","mor":"no net-rate resale","source":"https://www.thoroughlytravel.com/isla-espiritu-santo/"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-04","hero":{"query":"Espíritu Santo Island, Mexico"},"geo":{"lat":24.4714,"lng":-110.3325}}'::jsonb, 36),
  ('fernando-de-noronha-brazil', '10S', 'Fernando de Noronha, Brazil', 'Brazil', 'Volcanic archipelago, marine sanctuary, dolphin dawn', 'live', 'verified', 'oceanAerial', 'Northeast Beaches & Bahia', '{"liveaboard","tropical","romance","expedition"}', '{"tropical"}', '{"essential","comfort","premier"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":null,"safety":{"emergency":"190","advisory_level":"L2","advisory_why":"mainland urban crime + kidnapping; favelas L4. Archipelago itself is low-risk controlled-access marine park.","book_enabled":true,"bin":"freely bookable (L2)","consent_flow":false,"air_access_verified":true,"air_access":"FEN via Recife (REC) or Natal (NAT) only — Gol/Azul","no_fly_after_diving":"18-24h surface interval before FEN->mainland flight; plan dive-free last day","hyperbaric_chamber_onisland":true,"hyperbaric_note":"chamber adjacent to Hospital Sao Lucas (basic care); serious trauma/complex DCI requires mainland evac (Recife/Natal); weather can delay","remote_flag":true,"ocean_hazards":["strong currents/swell at outer-sea pinnacles & deep sites","riptides (worst Dec-Mar)","equatorial sun"],"protected_no_entry":["Baia dos Golfinhos (dolphin resting bay)"],"fcdo":{"posture":"AREA-RESTRICTED","quotes":[{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel Amazonas State FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the following river areas towards the west of Amazonas State: along the Amazonas (Amazon) River and its tributaries west of the town of Codajás and east of the town of Belém do Solimões in Amazonas State along any part of the Itaquaí River in Amazonas State along any part of the Japurá River or its tributaries in Amazonas State along the Rio Negro (Black River) and its tributaries north or west of the town of Barcelos in Amazonas State Find out more about why FCDO advises against travel ."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel: along the Amazonas (Amazon) River and its tributaries west of the town of Codajás and east of the town of Belém do Solimões in Amazonas State along any part of the Itaquaí River in Amazonas State along any part of the Japurá River or its tributaries in Amazonas State along the Rio Negro (Black River) and its tributaries north or west of the town of Barcelos in Amazonas State There are risks to travellers in river areas towards the west of Amazonas State, where Brazil shares borders with Colombia, Peru and Venezuela, due to criminal activity."}],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/brazil","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-05-11T12:32:48+01:00"}},"timing":{"dive_calendar":true,"peak_dive":"Aug-Nov (viz apex Sep-Oct)","peak_surf_highseason":"Dec-Mar","inflection":["late July","late November"],"fire_date":"curve-start minus 1-2 weeks (mid-late July for dive peak; mid-late November for Dec-Mar season)","booking_lead":"3-6 months for Dec-Mar (visitor cap + eco-tax + park permit)","offseason_fill":"Apr-Jun (rain hits surface, reef viz stays strong — diver''s value window)"},"jewels":[{"name":"Baia do Sancho","si_tag":"Tropical/Beaches","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.tripadvisor.com/Attraction_Review-g616328-d2391494-Reviews-Baia_do_Sancho-Fernando_de_Noronha_State_of_Pernambuco.html","si":"Tropical/Beaches","commission":"park ticket (pass-through) + commissionable boat/DMC day"},{"name":"Forte Boldro sunset viewpoint","si_tag":"Tropical/Beaches","tier":"essential","source":"https://postcardfromtaylor.com/blog/brazil/noronha-beaches/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"Tropical/Beaches","when":"year-round","commission":"guided island tour add-on"},{"name":"Ilha-tour boat trip","si_tag":"Tropical/Beaches","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.natalriograndedonorte.com/fernando-de-noronha-diving-and-snorkeling/","si":"Tropical/Beaches","commission":"commissionable boat operator/DMC"},{"name":"Corveta Ipiranga wreck (~62m)","si_tag":"diveglobal","tier":"premier","source":"https://bahia.ws/en/naufragio-da-corveta-ipiranga-no-arquipelago-de-fernando-de-noronha/","si":"diveglobal","commission":"premium tech-dive package"},{"name":"Caverna de Sapata (~18m)","si_tag":"diveglobal","tier":"comfort","source":"https://bahia.ws/en/mergulho-em-fernando-de-noronha/","si":"diveglobal","commission":"guided reef-dive package"},{"name":"Atalaia dive/snorkel zone (8-22m)","si_tag":"diveglobal","tier":"comfort","source":"https://bahia.ws/en/mergulho-em-fernando-de-noronha/","si":"diveglobal","commission":"dive-operator day trip"},{"name":"Baia dos Golfinhos dawn watch","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.tripadvisor.com/Attraction_Review-g616328-d2391494-Reviews-Baia_do_Sancho-Fernando_de_Noronha_State_of_Pernambuco.html","si":"expedition","commission":"guided dawn eco-tour (no-entry viewpoint)"},{"name":"Atalaia natural pool (guided/capped)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.parnanoronha.com.br/en/atrativos","hook":"reported variously. Treat as strictly capped, guide-mandatory, book-on-arrival. Confirm the day''s rule with ICMBio","si":"expedition","blurb":"reported variously. Treat as strictly capped, guide-mandatory, book-on-arrival. Confirm the day''s rule with ICMBio","commission":"ICMBio permit (pass-through) + guided eco add-on"},{"name":"Projeto Tamar visitor center","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.natalriograndedonorte.com/projeto-tamar-fernando-de-noronha/","si":"expedition","commission":"eco-tour visit inside guided day"}],"faq":[{"q":"When is the best time to dive Fernando de Noronha?","a":"August–November is the dive peak because the dry season delivers the clearest water and calmest seas, with the September–October visibility apex reaching up to ~50 m. April–June (rainy) is the diver''s value window — rain hits the surface, not the reef, so visibility stays strong and the island is quieter.","source":"planetaexo.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"liveaboard"},{"q":"How do you get to Baía do Sancho?","a":"Baía do Sancho is reached only by boat or by a staircase carved into the volcanic rock face, and a marine-park pass is required. It has been voted the best beach in the world by TripAdvisor travelers five times, which is why access is deliberately controlled.","source":"tripadvisor.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"tropical"},{"q":"Which is the best honeymoon pousada on Fernando de Noronha?","a":"Pousada Maravilha is consistently ranked the island''s top honeymoon hotel, with six sea-facing apartments plus bungalows with private hot tubs, an infinity pool, fine dining and a spa. Nannai Noronha (10 bungalows, private verandas, direct beach access) is the other ultra-tier couples pick.","source":"boutiquetravelexperts.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"Can you swim with the spinner dolphins at Baía dos Golfinhos?","a":"No — Baía dos Golfinhos is a no-entry protected dolphin resting bay: no descending, no swimming, no boats inside. Spinner dolphins are watched from a clifftop viewpoint, best at first light. This is a legal protection, not a suggestion.","source":"tripadvisor.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for?","a":"Remoteness and medical evacuation. Fernando de Noronha has a hyperbaric chamber adjacent to Hospital São Lucas, but the hospital provides basic emergency care only — serious trauma or complex decompression illness requires evacuation to the mainland (Recife/Natal), and weather can delay the flight. Carry insurance with medevac and dive conservatively.","source":"divejourney.io, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Is diving the Corveta Ipiranga wreck dangerous?","a":"It is technical / Extended-Range diving: the wreck sits at ~62 m off Ponta da Sapata, so operators require Nitrox plus ~50 logged dives and evaluation dives before permitting it, always with a pro. Recreational divers stay on shallower 8–22 m reef and cave sites. Because you leave only by air, observe an 18–24 h surface interval before your flight.","source":"bahia.ws, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"search_language":"pt-BR","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","freshness":"2026-07-07","local_keywords":["Fernando de Noronha mergulho","Baia do Sancho","taxa ambiental Noronha","taxa de preservacao ambiental Noronha 2026","Pousada Maravilha lua de mel","piscina natural Atalaia"],"hreflang":["en","pt-BR"]},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":null,"ultra":[{"name":"Pousada Maravilha","tier":"$$$$","lane":"Fora/Virtuoso","earning":"luxury commission + AOR; MoR on buyout","note":"island''s top honeymoon property"},{"name":"Nannai Noronha","tier":"$$$$","lane":"Fora/Virtuoso","earning":"luxury commission + dive attach; MoR villa-equivalent"},{"name":"Pousada Ze Maria","tier":"premier","lane":"premium romance","earning":"commissionable pousada + dining attach"},{"name":"Pousada Teju-Acu","tier":"premier","lane":"eco-luxury","earning":"commissionable boutique pousada + eco-tour attach"}],"source_verified":null,"hero":{"query":"Fernando de Noronha, Brazil, Brazil"},"geo":{"lat":-3.8547,"lng":-32.4248}}'::jsonb, 37),
  ('foz-do-iguacu-brazil', '10S', 'Foz do Iguaçu, Brazil', 'Brazil', 'Foz do Iguaçu', 'live', 'verified', 'mountainValley', 'Amazon, Pantanal & Iguaçu', '{"expedition","culture","romance"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":null,"safety":{"emergency":"190","emergency_medical":"192","emergency_fire":"193","advisory_level":"L2","book_enabled":true,"bin":"freely bookable (L2)","consent_flow":false,"air_access_verified":true,"air_access_note":"Foz do Iguaçu / Cataratas International Airport (IGU / SBFI), 13 km / ~8 mi from downtown, minutes from the park entrance; LATAM/Azul/Gol","hazards":["wet slippery falls walkways","Macuco boat full-soak / life vests mandatory","helicopter aviation","Argentine-side border crossing","Ciudad del Este / Paraguay-side petty crime","dengue"],"fcdo":{"posture":"AREA-RESTRICTED","quotes":[{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel Amazonas State FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the following river areas towards the west of Amazonas State: along the Amazonas (Amazon) River and its tributaries west of the town of Codajás and east of the town of Belém do Solimões in Amazonas State along any part of the Itaquaí River in Amazonas State along any part of the Japurá River or its tributaries in Amazonas State along the Rio Negro (Black River) and its tributaries north or west of the town of Barcelos in Amazonas State Find out more about why FCDO advises against travel ."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel: along the Amazonas (Amazon) River and its tributaries west of the town of Codajás and east of the town of Belém do Solimões in Amazonas State along any part of the Itaquaí River in Amazonas State along any part of the Japurá River or its tributaries in Amazonas State along the Rio Negro (Black River) and its tributaries north or west of the town of Barcelos in Amazonas State There are risks to travellers in river areas towards the west of Amazonas State, where Brazil shares borders with Colombia, Peru and Venezuela, due to criminal activity."}],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/brazil","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-05-11T12:32:48+01:00"}},"timing":{"peak":["Mar-Apr","Aug-Sep"],"peak_note":"Best flow + weather; Apr-May the single best window","summer_note":"Dec-Feb hot/rainiest/highest-water but most crowded","dry_note":"Jun-Aug cooler/calmer but lower flow","inflection":["~February (into Mar-Apr peak)","~July (into Aug-Sep peak)"],"fire_date":"curve-start minus 1-2 weeks — mid-to-late January (Mar-Apr travel) and late June (Aug-Sep travel)","off_season_fill":"Dec-Feb: sell max-roar high-water spectacle + Belmond honeymoon; bundle Itaipu-by-night + Parque das Aves"},"jewels":[{"si_tag":"expedition","name":"Trilha das Cataratas panoramic walkway + Devil''s Throat balcony","tier":"essential","source":"https://iguazufalls-tickets.org/what-to-see/iguazu-falls-brazil-side-viewpoints/ (Accessed 2026-07-07)","timing":"[''Mar-Apr'', ''Aug-Sep'']","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"The defining Brazilian-side experience: 1.4-km rim walk to the wide-angle Devil''s Throat view and panoramic elevator","si":"expedition","blurb":"The defining Brazilian-side experience: 1.4-km rim walk to the wide-angle Devil''s Throat view and panoramic elevator","when":"[''Mar-Apr'', ''Aug-Sep'']","commission":"park entry non-commissionable; guided-trail + transfer margin via DMC/OTA","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"si_tag":"expedition","name":"Macuco Safari — boat under the falls","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.viator.com/tours/Foz-do-Iguacu/Macuco-Safari-Boat-Ride/d970-7558P14 (Accessed 2026-07-07)","timing":"[''Mar-Apr'', ''Aug-Sep'']","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"The three-stage jungle-trail-boat run that soaks you beneath the cataracts","si":"expedition","blurb":"The three-stage jungle-trail-boat run that soaks you beneath the cataracts","when":"[''Mar-Apr'', ''Aug-Sep'']","commission":"OTA affiliate on operator margin; park-entry portion non-commissionable; from ~US$109/adult","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"si_tag":"expedition","name":"Helicopter over the falls (Helisul)","tier":"premier","source":"https://www.viator.com/tours/Foz-do-Iguacu/Panoramic-Helicopter-Flight-Iguazu-Falls-by-Helisul-Aviation/d970-216404P1 (Accessed 2026-07-07)","timing":"[''Mar-Apr'', ''Aug-Sep'']","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"10–12 min, both sides + Devil''s Throat in one frame, 7-seat cap","si":"expedition","blurb":"10–12 min, both sides + Devil''s Throat in one frame, 7-seat cap","when":"[''Mar-Apr'', ''Aug-Sep'']","commission":"OTA affiliate; US$120-166/pp; 7-seat cap","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"si_tag":"expedition","name":"Sunrise-before-crowds at the falls (in-park hotel)","tier":"luxury","source":"https://www.foratravel.com/trip-reports/A84HTP/a-stay-at-brazils-only-hotel-within-iguazu-falls-belmond-das-cataratas-saima-khan (Accessed 2026-07-07)","timing":"[''Mar-Apr'', ''Aug-Sep'']","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Only Belmond das Cataratas guests walk the trails before the 9am public opening — the falls, alone, at first light","si":"expedition","blurb":"Only Belmond das Cataratas guests walk the trails before the 9am public opening — the falls, alone, at first light","when":"[''Mar-Apr'', ''Aug-Sep'']","commission":"Belmond via Virtuoso/Fora consortium","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"si_tag":"romance","name":"Belmond das Cataratas terrace at sunset","tier":"luxury","source":"https://www.belmond.com/hotels/south-america/brazil/iguassu-falls/belmond-hotel-das-cataratas/location (Accessed 2026-07-07)","timing":"[''Mar-Apr'', ''Aug-Sep'']","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Caipirinha on the restaurant terrace as the sun sets behind the falls — the honeymoon set-piece","si":"romance","blurb":"Caipirinha on the restaurant terrace as the sun sets behind the falls — the honeymoon set-piece","when":"[''Mar-Apr'', ''Aug-Sep'']","commission":"hotel booking via preferred consortium","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"si_tag":"romance","name":"Argentine-side full-day Devil''s Throat catwalk","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.rebeccaandtheworld.com/visiting-iguazu-falls-argentina-brazil-sides/ (Accessed 2026-07-07)","timing":"[''Mar-Apr'', ''Aug-Sep'']","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"The 1.1-km catwalk to the lip of Garganta del Diablo — the overwhelming close-range half of the wonder, framed as a romance day-adventure","si":"romance","blurb":"The 1.1-km catwalk to the lip of Garganta del Diablo — the overwhelming close-range half of the wonder, framed as a romance day-adventure","when":"[''Mar-Apr'', ''Aug-Sep'']","commission":"guided cross-border transfer via DMC (border-crossing logistics = margin)","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"si_tag":"culture","name":"Parque das Aves","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.tripadvisor.com/Attraction_Review-g303444-d737277-Reviews-Parque_das_Aves-Foz_do_Iguacu_State_of_Parana.html (Accessed 2026-07-07)","timing":"[''Mar-Apr'', ''Aug-Sep'']","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"beside the national park, holds more than 1,320 birds across roughly 143 species in 16.5 hectares of Atlantic Rainforest","si":"culture","blurb":"beside the national park, holds more than 1,320 birds across roughly 143 species in 16.5 hectares of Atlantic Rainforest","when":"[''Mar-Apr'', ''Aug-Sep'']","commission":"OTA admission + guided-tour margin","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"si_tag":"culture","name":"Itaipu Dam Illuminated night tour","tier":"essential","source":"https://turismoitaipu.com.br/en/blog/Itaipu-tour-illuminated-Foz-at-night/ (Accessed 2026-07-07)","timing":"[''Mar-Apr'', ''Aug-Sep'']","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"sold via the official Itaipu tourism channel and OTAs; a strong length-of-stay extender","si":"culture","blurb":"sold via the official Itaipu tourism channel and OTAs; a strong length-of-stay extender","when":"[''Mar-Apr'', ''Aug-Sep'']","commission":"official Itaipu tourism channel + OTA","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"si_tag":"culture","name":"Triple-frontier viewpoint (Marco das Três Fronteiras)","tier":"essential","source":"https://greydynamics.com/gangsters-paradise-south-americas-triple-frontier/ (Accessed 2026-07-07)","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"culture","when":"year-round","commission":"guided-tour margin; kept on the safe Brazilian bank away from Ciudad del Este","accessed":"2026-07-07"}],"faq":[{"q":"When is the best time to visit the Brazilian side of Iguaçu Falls?","a":"March–April and August–September are the sweet spots — comfortable 20–30°C, still-high water from the summer rains, and far smaller crowds than the December–February peak; April–May is widely called the single best window, with near-full flow, cooled temperatures and thinned crowds.","source":"iguazufalls-tickets.org, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Why stay at the Belmond Hotel das Cataratas?","a":"Because it is the only hotel inside Brazil''s Iguaçu National Park, its guests get the falls essentially alone — walking the trails before the 9am public opening and after the 5pm closing, the dawn-and-dusk private-falls access that no city hotel can match.","source":"foratravel.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"What''s worth doing besides the falls themselves?","a":"Two standouts extend the stay: the Itaipu Dam \"Illuminated\" night tour lights one of the world''s largest hydroelectric plants with 747 spotlights and 112 luminaires, and Parque das Aves next to the park immerses you among 1,320+ birds across roughly 143 species.","source":"turismoitaipu.com.br, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for around the falls?","a":"The tri-border corridor: the Brazil–Argentina–Paraguay triple frontier is a known smuggling and money-laundering zone, but the Iguazu tourist corridor stays accessible with normal precautions — it''s the Paraguay-side Ciudad del Este shopping run that carries elevated petty-crime and after-dark risk, so advise clients away from it unless escorted.","source":"greydynamics.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Is the Macuco Safari boat trip dangerous?","a":"No, when run with the operator: it''s a guided-only, three-stage run of roughly 1 hr 45 min (about 30 min on the water) with mandatory life vests issued at the dock — expect to get completely soaked, so leave anything not waterproof behind.","source":"iguazufalls.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Foz do Iguaçu, Brazil — Iguaçu Falls Panoramic Side, In-Park Belmond & Macuco Safari | TravelWell.World","meta_description":"Plan the Brazilian side of Iguaçu Falls — the wide-angle Devil''s Throat, the boat under the cataracts, the only in-park hotel, and how to time your visit for peak flow.","search_language":"pt-BR","local_keywords":["Cataratas do Iguaçu","Macuco Safari","Parque das Aves","Trilha das Cataratas","Garganta do Diabo","Usina de Itaipu iluminada","melhor época para visitar as Cataratas"],"long_tail_en":["Iguaçu Falls Brazil side vs Argentina side","best time to visit Iguaçu Falls Brazilian side","only hotel inside Iguaçu National Park Brazil","Macuco Safari boat under the falls","helicopter tour over Iguaçu Falls","is Foz do Iguaçu safe to visit"],"hreflang":["en","pt-BR"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","freshness":"2026-07-07","primary_keyword":"Foz do Iguaçu"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"expedition","status":"live"},{"si":"culture","status":"live"},{"si":"romance","status":"live"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Belmond Hotel das Cataratas","side":"Brazil (in-park)","earning":"consortium commission on room + F&B + spa + VIP amenity/upgrade value","mor":"hotel (agent AOR via Fora/Virtuoso)","tier":"ULTRA","hook":"only hotel inside the Brazilian NP; dawn/dusk private falls access before 9am and after 5pm"},{"name":"Loi Suites Iguazú","side":"Argentina (cross-ref, outside park on approach road)","earning":"consortium commission via Scott Dunn / andBeyond-class partners","mor":"hotel","tier":"ULTRA (cross-ref, not primary)","hook":"5-star jungle lodge, 162 units on wooden bridges through Iryapú forest; note Sheraton Iguazú is the in-park Argentine option"}],"source_verified":null,"hero":{"query":"Foz do Iguaçu, Brazil, Brazil"},"geo":{"lat":-25.5163,"lng":-54.5854}}'::jsonb, 38),
  ('galapagos-islands-ecuador', '10S', 'The Galápagos Islands', 'Ecuador', 'Liveaboard weeks and island crossings', 'live', 'verified', 'oceanAerial', 'Andes (Quito) & Galápagos', '{"liveaboard","expedition"}', '{}', '{"comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["Darwin and Wolf islands are reachable ONLY by liveaboard; most trips run 7 nights with up to 4 dives/day.","Galapagos is one of the only places on earth to reliably dive with whale sharks (10-12m adults), June-November, peak August-September.","During the June-November cool season ~90% of monitored hammerheads stay in the reserve; schools aggregate along the thermocline ~20-30m.","Galapagos National Park entry fee doubled to US$200 per foreign adult on 2024-08-01; INGALA/CGREG transit card (TCT) is a separate ~US$20-30.","Access is via Baltra/Seymour (GPS) or San Cristobal (SCY) on Avianca/LATAM flights from Quito (UIO) or Guayaquil (GYE) only."],"safety":{"emergency":"911","marine_vhf":"Channel 16","hyperbaric_chamber":"Puerto Ayora, Santa Cruz — Protesub S.A. / SSS Recompression Chamber Network (DAN referral center), 24/7, +593 5 252-6911. Only chamber in the islands; many hours by boat from Darwin/Wolf; serious cases medevac to mainland or US.","advisory_level":"L2","advisory_date":"2025-10-14","advisory_codes":"C (Crime) / T (Terrorism) / U (Unrest) / K (Kidnapping) — mainland-driven; islands not a named area","book_enabled":true,"bin":"freely bookable (L2)","consent_flow":"none (BIN 4 — standard L2 disclosure only)","l2_disclosure":true,"state_dept_carveout":"Galápagos and Quito explicitly NOT designated restricted; L4 zones are mainland-only (Esmeraldas city+north, Guayaquil south of Portete de Tarqui Ave., Duran, Huaquillas/Arenillas, Quevedo/Quinsaloma/Pueblo Viejo)","air_access_verified":true,"air_access":"GPS (Baltra/Seymour) and SCY (San Cristobal) via UIO (Quito) or GYE (Guayaquil) on Avianca/LATAM","no_fly_after_diving":"12h single no-deco / 18h multi-day repetitive / 24h recommended buffer before the island-to-mainland flight (note Quito altitude ~2,850m)","medevac_note":"State Dept warns serious illness/injury typically requires medical evacuation; recommends evacuation insurance $60,000+","other":"open-Pacific seasickness (long overnight Darwin/Wolf crossings roughest); extreme equatorial sun; DAN dive insurance with evac coverage effectively mandatory","fcdo":{"posture":"AREA-RESTRICTED","quotes":[{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel Coastal Region FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the Coastal Region provinces of: Esmeraldas Manabí Santa Elena Guayas El Oro Los Ríos Santo Domingo de los Tsáchilas This does not apply to airside transit within Guayaquil Airport in Guayas province."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to areas within 20km of the Ecuador-Colombia border, except for these areas in Carchi province: El Ángel Ecological Reserve Rumichaca border crossing the town of Tulcán the Pan-American Highway Find out more about why FCDO advises against travel ."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to Guayaquil, except for airside transit through the airport."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to those provinces) and get local advice on where to visit."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the Coastal Region provinces of: Esmeraldas Manabi Santa Elena El Oro Los Ríos Santo Domingo de los Tsáchilas This is due to a high level of gang-related violence linked to the presence of organised crime relating to the production and trafficking of illegal drugs."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the Coastal Region province of Guayas, except: airside transit within Guayaquil Airport in Guayas province."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to areas within 20km of the Ecuador-Colombia border, except for these areas in Carchi province: El Ángel Ecological Reserve Rumichaca border crossing the town of Tulcán the Pan-American Highway This is due to the presence of organised crime linked to the production and trafficking of drugs."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel."}],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/ecuador","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-07-10T10:44:44+01:00"}},"timing":{"type":"dive-calendar-two-season","dive_calendar":true,"warm_snorkel_season":"December-May (warmer water ~25-27C, calm seas, best snorkel/land wildlife; family + honeymoon)","big_marine_dive_season":"June-November (cool ~16-24C, strong currents; hammerhead schools + whale sharks at Darwin & Wolf)","peak":"July-August + whale-shark peak August-September + mid-December-early-January holidays","dive_curve_start":"2026-06-01","warm_curve_start":"2026-12-01","booking_lead_months":"6-12 (top liveaboard cabins + premium expedition suites; whale-shark weeks and holidays sell first)","shoulder_off_season_fill":"April-May and September-October","fire_date":"2026-05-18","trigger_date":"2026-05-18","secondary_fire_date":"2026-11-15","sharpen_note":"sharpen on live tracking — Aggressor / expedition-cruise availability feeds + hammerhead & whale-shark sighting logs; upwelling onset and pelagic aggregation shift yearly"},"jewels":[{"name":"Darwin''s Arch / Darwin Island","si_tag":"Dive Liveaboards/GEA","tier":"premier","source":"https://www.naturetripper.com/articles/whale-sharks-galapagos","timing":"July-August + whale-shark peak August-September + mid-December-early-January holidays","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"Dive Liveaboards/GEA","when":"July-August + whale-shark peak August-September + mid-December-early-January holidays","commission":"own-CLIA / TCI Land Agency lane (Galápagos Aggressor III) — the moat"},{"name":"Wolf Island","si_tag":"Dive Liveaboards/GEA","tier":"premier","source":"https://www.dive-the-world.com/posts/darwin-wolf/galapagos-islands-diving-trips-darwin-and-wolf-islands.php","timing":"July-August + whale-shark peak August-September + mid-December-early-January holidays","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"Dive Liveaboards/GEA","when":"July-August + whale-shark peak August-September + mid-December-early-January holidays","commission":"own-CLIA liveaboard lane — the moat"},{"name":"Gordon Rocks (off Santa Cruz)","si_tag":"Dive Liveaboards/GEA","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.aggressor.com/kbyg_document/galapagos","timing":"July-August + whale-shark peak August-September + mid-December-early-January holidays","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"Dive Liveaboards/GEA","when":"July-August + whale-shark peak August-September + mid-December-early-January holidays","commission":"own-CLIA liveaboard lane or AFF day-boat from Puerto Ayora"},{"name":"Kicker Rock / León Dormido (off San Cristóbal)","si_tag":"Dive Liveaboards/GEA","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.oars.com/adventures/galapagos-origins-of-species/","timing":"July-August + whale-shark peak August-September + mid-December-early-January holidays","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"Dive Liveaboards/GEA","when":"July-August + whale-shark peak August-September + mid-December-early-January holidays","commission":"own-CLIA liveaboard lane or AFF day-operator from San Cristóbal"},{"name":"Cabo Marshall / Cabo Douglas & Punta Vicente Roca (Isabela/Fernandina)","si_tag":"liveaboard","tier":"premier","source":"https://www.aggressor.com/kbyg_document/galapagos","timing":"July-August + whale-shark peak August-September + mid-December-early-January holidays","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"liveaboard","when":"July-August + whale-shark peak August-September + mid-December-early-January holidays","commission":"own-CLIA liveaboard lane"},{"name":"Bartolomé — Pinnacle Rock","si_tag":"GEA/Romance","tier":"luxury","source":"https://ecolodgesanywhere.com/galapagos-islands/","timing":"July-August + whale-shark peak August-September + mid-December-early-January holidays","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"GEA/Romance","when":"July-August + whale-shark peak August-September + mid-December-early-January holidays","commission":"Fora/Virtuoso expedition-cruise lane"},{"name":"Española — Punta Suárez (waved albatross)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"luxury","source":"https://ecolodgesanywhere.com/galapagos-islands/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"expedition","when":"year-round","commission":"Fora/Virtuoso expedition-cruise lane"},{"name":"Genovesa — Bird Island","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"luxury","source":"https://ecolodgesanywhere.com/galapagos-islands/","timing":"July-August + whale-shark peak August-September + mid-December-early-January holidays","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"expedition","when":"July-August + whale-shark peak August-September + mid-December-early-January holidays","commission":"Fora/Virtuoso expedition-cruise lane"},{"name":"Charles Darwin Research Station + giant tortoises (Santa Cruz)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Puerto_Ayora","timing":"July-August + whale-shark peak August-September + mid-December-early-January holidays","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"expedition","when":"July-August + whale-shark peak August-September + mid-December-early-January holidays","commission":"AFF/day lane add-on to a Fora hotel/cruise booking"},{"name":"Isabela — Sierra Negra volcano & Galápagos penguins","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.kimkim.com/c/galapagos-snorkeling-wildlife-tour-7-days","si":"expedition","commission":"AFF day-operator lane; Fora if bundled in a land package"},{"name":"Los Túneles (Cabo Rosa, Isabela)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.kimkim.com/c/galapagos-snorkeling-wildlife-tour-7-days","timing":"July-August + whale-shark peak August-September + mid-December-early-January holidays","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"expedition","when":"July-August + whale-shark peak August-September + mid-December-early-January holidays","commission":"AFF day-operator lane"},{"name":"Tortuga Bay (Santa Cruz)","si_tag":"GEA/Romance","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.kimkim.com/c/galapagos-snorkeling-wildlife-tour-7-days","timing":"July-August + whale-shark peak August-September + mid-December-early-January holidays","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"GEA/Romance","when":"July-August + whale-shark peak August-September + mid-December-early-January holidays","commission":"AFF/day lane (self-guided) add-on to a Fora hotel booking"}],"faq":[{"q":"How dangerous is diving Darwin and Wolf — can beginners do it?","a":"No — these are advanced dives, not a beginner destination. Reputable operators gate Darwin/Wolf on Advanced Open Water certification plus logged current/cold-water experience: divers hook onto ledges in ripping current at 20–30 m in 16–24 °C water, far from support. Gordon Rocks and Kicker Rock are the intermediate-to-advanced warm-ups.","source":"aggressor.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"liveaboard"},{"q":"How long should I wait to fly after diving the Galápagos?","a":"Plan a full 18–24 hours before the island-to-mainland flight. A liveaboard week is repetitive multi-day diving (DAN: 18 h minimum, 24 h recommended), and Quito sits at ~2,850 m — so never book a same-day-as-last-dive flight. The only hyperbaric chamber is in Puerto Ayora, hours by boat from Darwin/Wolf, so DAN evacuation insurance is effectively mandatory.","source":"DAN guidance via sssnetwork.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"dive-safety"},{"q":"When is the best time to dive for hammerheads and whale sharks?","a":"June–November — the cool, plankton-rich season — is the big-animal window, with whale sharks peaking August–September, because the Humboldt upwelling drops water to 16–24 °C and concentrates pelagic life; ~90% of monitored hammerheads stay in the reserve then, schooling in the hundreds. Expect cooler water and stronger current.","source":"galapagossharkdiving.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"liveaboard"},{"q":"Do I need a cruise, or can I stay on land?","a":"Both work, but the iconic sites need a boat. Darwin and Wolf are liveaboard-only, and by park rule every visitor-site landing must be led by a licensed naturalist guide. Land-based island-hopping (Santa Cruz, Isabela) covers tortoises, Tortuga Bay and day dives; the deep wildlife (Española albatross, Genovesa seabirds) needs an expedition cruise.","source":"oars.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"What''s the best Galápagos trip for a honeymoon?","a":"A small all-suite expedition yacht or the highlands Pikaia Lodge. The warm season (Dec–May, water 25–27 °C, calm seas) is the easiest for first-timers and snorkeling; book 6–12 months ahead because the top cabins and suites — and holiday sailings — sell out first.","source":"galapagossharkdiving.com / dive-the-world.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"romance"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Galápagos Diving & Expedition Cruises — Darwin & Wolf Liveaboards, Hammerheads, Whale Sharks | TravelWell.World","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","content_freshness":"2026-07-07","search_language":"es-EC","local_keywords":["Galapagos liveaboard diving","Darwin Wolf hammerheads","Galapagos cruise","Galapagos whale shark diving","Galapagos Aggressor III","best time to dive Galapagos","Galapagos expedition cruise","islas Galápagos crucero","bucear Galápagos","crucero de buceo Galápagos","tiburón ballena Galápagos","no fly after diving Galapagos"],"hreflang":["en","es-EC"]},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":["liveaboard","expedition"],"ultra":[{"name":"Aqua Mare (Aqua Expeditions) — 16-guest superyacht","tier":"ultra","mor":"Fora / Virtuoso luxury-cruise lane; full-yacht buyout = villa-equivalent","source":"https://www.luxurytraveladvisor.com/cruises/wild-things"},{"name":"Silversea Silver Origin — 100-guest ultra-luxury expedition","tier":"luxury-ultra","mor":"Fora / Virtuoso luxury-cruise lane (Virtuoso-preferred)","source":"https://www.luxurytraveladvisor.com/cruises/wild-things"},{"name":"Celebrity Flora — 100-guest all-suite expedition","tier":"luxury-ultra","mor":"Fora / Virtuoso luxury-cruise lane","source":"https://www.luxurytraveladvisor.com/cruises/wild-things"},{"name":"Ecoventura Origin / Theory / Evolve — 20-guest all-suite (Relais & Châteaux)","tier":"luxury-ultra","mor":"Fora / Virtuoso luxury-cruise lane (Relais & Châteaux)","source":"https://www.luxurytraveladvisor.com/cruises/wild-things"},{"name":"Pikaia Lodge (Santa Cruz highlands, Relais & Châteaux + private yacht)","tier":"luxury-ultra","mor":"Fora lane (host-agency IATA)","source":"https://www.mrandmrssmith.com/luxury-hotels/pikaia-lodge"},{"name":"Private full-yacht charter (Aggressor III buyout / all-suite expedition buyout)","tier":"ultra","mor":"own-CLIA / TCI Land Agency lane — convertible affiliate->commissioned-agent (the moat)","source":"https://www.aggressor.com/destination/galapagos"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-07","hero":{"query":"The Galápagos Islands, Ecuador"},"geo":{"lat":-0.9538,"lng":-90.9656}}'::jsonb, 39),
  ('granada-nicaragua', '10S', 'Granada, Nicaragua', 'Nicaragua', 'Granada', 'live', 'verified', 'kyoto', 'Nicaragua', '{"culture"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":null,"safety":{"emergency":"118","emergency_all":{"police":"118","ambulance_red_cross":"128","fire":"115 / 911 (cell)","tourist_line":"101"},"advisory_date":"2026-05-14","advisory_codes":["C","H","D","O"],"book_enabled":false,"bin":"NO SAFE ZONE (content-only)","content_only":true,"redirect_eligible":true,"consent_flow":null,"trauma":"limited outside Managua; comprehensive care Managua-only → US medevac","founder_review_flag":"WHY = country-wide political detention (targets perceived govt opponents/NGO/journalist/dual-national/property); may not reach a typical short-stay Granada tourist — reconsideration is a founder/attorney call, NOT a CC call. Flagged, not decided.","source":"https://travel.state.gov/content/travel/en/traveladvisories/traveladvisories/nicaragua-travel-advisory.html + Accessed 2026-07-07"},"timing":{"peak":"Nov–Apr (dry season)","inflection":"May & Oct shoulder; Jun–Sep wet/low","off_season":"Jun–Sep wetter, quieter","fire_date":"held — pending advisory clearance + founder/attorney"},"jewels":[{"name":"Catedral de Granada","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://onaroadtonowhere.com/2025/02/25/granada-nicaragua-a-colonial-beauty-that-might-steal-your-heart/ + Accessed 2026-07-07","timing":"Nov–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the yellow-and-white bell towers and crimson domes over Parque Central","si":"culture","blurb":"the yellow-and-white bell towers and crimson domes over Parque Central","when":"Nov–Apr","commission":"non-commissionable","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"name":"Calle La Calzada","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.tripadvisor.com/Attraction_Review-g580113-d2707513-Reviews-Calle_La_Calzada-Granada_Granada_Department.html + Accessed 2026-07-07","timing":"Nov–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the lively colonial spine of the city; colorful façades, restaurants and bars, live music and salsa after sunset","si":"culture","blurb":"the lively colonial spine of the city; colorful façades, restaurants and bars, live music and salsa after sunset","when":"Nov–Apr","commission":"non-commissionable","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"name":"Las Isletas (kayak/boat)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.viator.com/Nicaragua-attractions/Islets-of-Granada-Las-Isletas-de-Granada/d4499-a6931 + Accessed 2026-07-07","hook":"lifejackets, weather-aware; a captained boat is the norm. Content","si":"expedition","blurb":"lifejackets, weather-aware; a captained boat is the norm. Content","commission":"dormant","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"name":"Mombacho cloud-forest + canopy","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.viator.com/tours/Granada/Mombacho-Volcano-Cloud-Forest/d4853-69457P3 + Accessed 2026-07-07","timing":"Nov–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"always with a park-authorized guide on the 4x4 + Crater Trail; cloud-forest footing is wet and steep. Content","si":"expedition","blurb":"always with a park-authorized guide on the 4x4 + Crater Trail; cloud-forest footing is wet and steep. Content","when":"Nov–Apr","commission":"dormant","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"name":"Masaya active lava-lake (night) + Masaya market","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.tripadvisor.com/AttractionProductReview-g580113-d12935426-Masaya_Volcano_Night_Tour_and_Apoyo_Lagoon-Granada_Granada_Department.html + Accessed 2026-07-07","hook":"molten glow from the crater rim; pair with Masaya artisan market by day for hammocks, ceramics, leather","si":"expedition","blurb":"molten glow from the crater rim; pair with Masaya artisan market by day for hammocks, ceramics, leather","commission":"dormant","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"name":"Laguna de Apoyo swim","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://hiddennicaragua.com/2022/07/10/apoyo-lagoon-nicaragua/ + Accessed 2026-07-07","hook":"protected caldera lake, no motorboats, clean water; deep and steep-sided — swim near shore/lakeside spots. Content","si":"expedition","blurb":"protected caldera lake, no motorboats, clean water; deep and steep-sided — swim near shore/lakeside spots. Content","commission":"dormant","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"name":"León day trip","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://bbqboy.net/visiting-granada-volcan-masaya-and-laguna-de-apoyo-nicaragua/ + Accessed 2026-07-07","timing":"Nov–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Granada''s colonial rival/sibling city, an easy day out for churches and revolutionary-mural history","si":"culture","blurb":"Granada''s colonial rival/sibling city, an easy day out for churches and revolutionary-mural history","when":"Nov–Apr","commission":"dormant","accessed":"2026-07-07"}],"faq":[{"q":"Why is Granada worth visiting?","a":"Granada is the oldest city in Nicaragua and the oldest colonial city on the American mainland, settled in 1524 by conquistador Francisco Hernández de Córdoba. It claims to be the first European-established city on the mainland of the Americas, and its well-preserved colonial grid of pastel façades is the whole point of coming.","source":"costarica.org, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"What are the best outdoor things to do around Granada?","a":"The signature outings are volcanoes and water. Las Isletas — 365 islets flung into Lake Nicaragua by a Mombacho eruption — are toured by boat or kayak; Mombacho''s cloud-forest is reached by 4x4 to a Crater Trail hike plus a canopy zip course; and Masaya''s night tour puts you at a crater-rim platform above an active lava lake.","source":"viator.com; tripadvisor.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Where''s the best place to swim near Granada?","a":"Laguna de Apoyo, a crater lake about 25 minutes from Granada, is said to be the cleanest place to swim in all of Nicaragua because no motorboats are allowed on it. Day passes to lakeside spots run around $10 and include kayaks and loungers.","source":"hiddennicaragua.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Is Granada a good honeymoon destination?","a":"Yes, on paper it is a natural romance set — private-island lodges, rooftop sunsets over Cocibolca, pastel streets. The ultra anchor is Jicaro Island Lodge, a National Geographic Unique Lodge with 9 two-story \"treehouse\" casitas on a private Las Isletas islet, with lakeside yoga and three multi-course meals included.","source":"jicaroisland.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for?","a":"Wrongful detention is the headline gatekeeper. Per the State Department, US nationals — including dual Nicaraguan-US citizens — are at serious risk of wrongful detention and may be held for years without due process, and authorities may seize property or search phones for anti-government content. A secondary risk is healthcare: comprehensive care exists only in Managua.","source":"travel.state.gov, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Are the volcano hikes and lake trips dangerous?","a":"The activities themselves are guided and manageable, but they are content-only under the Level 3 advisory. Mombacho and Masaya are done with a park-authorized or licensed guide (volcanic-gas exposure and timed entry make it mandatory at Masaya), and Las Isletas boating requires lifejackets because Cocibolca can chop up fast.","source":"travel.state.gov, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Granada, Nicaragua Travel Guide — Colonial Jewel, Las Isletas & Volcanoes | TravelWell.World","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","freshness":"2026-07-07","search_language":"es-NI","local_keywords":["qué hacer en Granada Nicaragua","Las Isletas","Volcán Masaya","Volcán Mombacho bosque nuboso","Laguna de Apoyo nadar","Catedral de Granada","Calle La Calzada"],"hreflang":["en","es-NI"],"primary_keyword":"Granada"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"culture","status":"live"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Jicaro Island Lodge","note":"NatGeo Unique Lodge, 9 treehouse casitas on private Las Isletas islet, spa/yoga, near-carbon-neutral","price_tier":"$$$$","commission_path":"dormant","source":"https://jicaroisland.com/ + Accessed 2026-07-07"},{"name":"Tribal Hotel","note":"boutique retreat in colonial core, garden + pool","price_tier":"$$$","commission_path":"dormant","source":"https://www.lightfoottravel.com/us/property/tribal-hotel + Accessed 2026-07-07"},{"name":"La Gran Francia / Hotel Plaza Colón","note":"restored colonial-mansion luxury on/near Parque Central","price_tier":"$$$","commission_path":"dormant","source":"https://voicesoftravel.com/where-to-stay-in-granada-nicaragua/ + Accessed 2026-07-07"}],"source_verified":null,"hero":{"query":"Granada, Nicaragua, Nicaragua"},"geo":{"lat":11.9344,"lng":-85.956}}'::jsonb, 40),
