OW","hook":"~8,000 textile pieces from 180+ Indigenous communities; huipiles, cortes, ceremonial garments; open Mon–Fri 9–5, Sat 9–1","si":"culture","blurb":"~8,000 textile pieces from 180+ Indigenous communities; huipiles, cortes, ceremonial garments; open Mon–Fri 9–5, Sat 9–1","when":"November–March + Semana Santa","commission":"admission non-commissionable → guided textile tour + Antigua/Atitlán artisan retail linkage","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"name":"Museo Nacional de Arqueología y Etnología","si_tag":"culture","zone":"13","tier":"essential","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Guatemala_City (Accessed 2026-07-06)","timing":"November–March + Semana Santa","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","when":"November–March + Semana Santa","commission":"bundle into DMC city tour","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"name":"Zone 1 Historic Center (Palacio Nacional, Cathedral, Mercado Central)","si_tag":"culture","zone":"1","tier":"essential","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Guatemala_City (Accessed 2026-07-06)","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"the founding civic core: National Palace, Cathedral, and the underground artisan market","si":"culture","blurb":"the founding civic core: National Palace, Cathedral, and the underground artisan market","when":"year-round","commission":"commissioned daytime historic-center walking tour via DMC","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"name":"Paseo Cayalá / Ciudad Cayalá","si_tag":"Lifestyle/Dining","zone":"16","tier":"comfort","source":"https://livinginguatemala.com/neighborhoods/zona-16-cayala/ (Accessed 2026-07-06)","timing":"November–March + Semana Santa","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"Lifestyle/Dining","when":"November–March + Semana Santa","commission":"non-bookable district → hotel night + DMC evening transfer","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"name":"Zona Viva dining","si_tag":"Lifestyle/Dining","zone":"10","tier":"comfort","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Guatemala_City (Accessed 2026-07-06)","timing":"November–March + Semana Santa","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"Lifestyle/Dining","when":"November–March + Semana Santa","commission":"hotel-package upsell","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"name":"Antigua Guatemala transfer/day-trip","si_tag":"Culture & Heritage / Adventure","zone":"onward (~45 min)","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.lonelyplanet.com/articles/best-time-to-visit-guatemala (Accessed 2026-07-06)","timing":"November–March + Semana Santa","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"colonial UNESCO city; the real reason GC exists as a gateway","si":"Culture & Heritage / Adventure","blurb":"colonial UNESCO city; the real reason GC exists as a gateway","when":"November–March + Semana Santa","commission":"commissioned DMC transfer + Antigua land package (primary revenue move)","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"name":"Pacaya Volcano day-trip","si_tag":"adventure","zone":"onward (~1.5–2 hr)","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.martsam.com/ (Accessed 2026-07-06)","timing":"November–March + Semana Santa","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"adventure","when":"November–March + Semana Santa","commission":"commissioned DMC guided excursion","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"name":"La Aurora Zoo","si_tag":"Family/Layover","zone":"13","tier":"essential","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Guatemala_City (Accessed 2026-07-06)","si":"Family/Layover","commission":"non-commissionable admission; long-layover add-on","accessed":"2026-07-06"}],"faq":[{"q":"Should I stay in Guatemala City or head straight to Antigua?","a":"Treat Guatemala City as a 1–2-night stopover, not a leisure anchor. It''s the international gateway — La Aurora (Central America''s 4th-busiest, 4,919,850 pax in 2024) sits in Zone 13, ~45–60 minutes (~40–45 km) from Antigua — so most travelers rest a night, then road out to the country''s true anchors.","source":"en.wikipedia.org, Accessed 2026-07-06","si_tag":null},{"q":"Is Guatemala City worth a stop for museums?","a":"Yes, for a half-day. The museum cluster is genuinely first-rate: Museo Popol Vuh holds one of the country''s best pre-Hispanic and colonial-art collections, and Museo Ixchel holds ~8,000 textile pieces from 180+ Indigenous communities, both on the UFM campus in the safe Zone 10.","source":"museoixchel.org, Accessed 2026-07-06","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"How do I get from the airport safely?","a":"Use arranged or vetted transport, or Uber — never a street-hailed taxi. Move from La Aurora (Zone 13) to Zone 10/14 lodging on pre-arranged transport, avoid walking at night in unfamiliar zones, and ride the onward Antigua/Atitlán/Tikal handoff on a vetted shuttle or the DMC''s own transport.","source":"travel.state.gov, Accessed 2026-07-06","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Guatemala City Travel Guide — La Aurora Gateway, Zona Viva & Safe-Zone Stopover | TravelWell.World","meta_description":"Accurate guide to Guatemala City as the international gateway (GUA) to Antigua, Atitlán & Tikal — Zona Viva stays, museum cluster, safety zones, Level 3 route-around.","search_language":["en","es-GT"],"local_keywords":["qué hacer en Ciudad de Guatemala","Zona Viva hoteles","escala Guatemala City","Museo Ixchel Zona 10","traslado aeropuerto La Aurora a Antigua","zonas seguras Ciudad de Guatemala"],"long_tail_en":["Guatemala City stopover before Antigua","is Guatemala City safe Zona Viva Zone 10","La Aurora airport to Antigua transfer","best hotels Zona Viva Guatemala City","Guatemala travel advisory Zone 18 Villa Nueva"],"hreflang":["en","es-GT"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","content_freshness":"2026-07-06"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":["Culture & Heritage (future)"],"ultra":[{"property":"Westin Camino Real (Zone 10)","play":"premier gateway night","channel":"Fora/Virtuoso consortia; else GDS commissioned","mor":"Fora advisor","tier":"premier"},{"property":"InterContinental Guatemala (Zone 10)","play":"business-luxury gateway","channel":"IHG consortia / Fora","mor":"Fora/consortia","tier":"premier"},{"property":"Barceló Guatemala City (Zone 10)","play":"upper premier gateway","channel":"consortia / GDS","mor":"consortia","tier":"premier"},{"property":"Hyatt Centric (Zone 10)","play":"lifestyle premier gateway","channel":"Hyatt Privé / Fora","mor":"Fora/Privé","tier":"premier"},{"property":"Antigua boutique-colonial base (REDIRECT)","play":"the true ultra stay — GC is transit","channel":"Fora/Virtuoso Antigua portfolio","mor":"Fora advisor","tier":"ultra"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-06","hero":{"query":"Guatemala City, Guatemala"},"geo":{"lat":14.6349,"lng":-90.5069}}'::jsonb, 45),
  ('holbox-mexico', '10S', 'Holbox', 'Mexico', 'Holbox whale sharks', 'live', 'verified', 'tropicalBeach', 'Quintana Roo (Cancún & Riviera Maya)', '{"expedition","romance","ocean","wildlife"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["Whale-shark season mid-May to mid-Sep (official May 15-Sep 17), gov-enforced","Snorkel-only, no-touch; two swimmers + guide per turn; CONANP-certified operators only","Car-free island reached by ferry from Chiquila; golf carts/mopeds only","Bioluminescence at Punta Cocos on dark nights (western tip)","Inside Yum Balam Flora & Fauna Protection Area (~90% of Yucatan endemic birds)"],"safety":{"emergency":"911","hospital":"small local health center on-island; serious cases evac by ferry+road to Cancun private hospitals or air-evac","advisory_level":"L2","malaria":"effectively none in tourist zone","dengue":"active - Quintana Roo among highest-activity states 2026; chikungunya/Zika circulate; mangrove mosquitoes","water":"bottled/purified only","hurricane":"Jun-Nov - overlaps whale-shark peak","whale_shark":"SNORKEL ONLY, no-touch; life jackets typically mandatory; seasickness common (open water); biodegradable reef-safe sunscreen mandatory; CONANP-licensed operator required","fcdo":{"posture":"AREA-RESTRICTED","quotes":[{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel State of Baja California FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tijuana, except: airside transit through Tijuana airport the Cross Border Xpress bridge from the airport linking terminals across the Mexican-US border the federal toll road 1D and Via Rápida through Tijuana to the border FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tecate in Baja California, including roads between Tijuana and Tecate."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Chihuahua, except: the city of Chihuahua the border crossing in Ciudad