lto Mezquitic San Martin de Bolaños Santa Maria de los Ángeles Totatiche Villa Guerrero State of Colima FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Colima, except the city of Manzanillo accessed by sea or air via the Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport, and direct travel via road 200 from the airport to Manzanillo."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Guerrero, except the town of Zihuatanejo/Ixtapa accessed by air."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to within 40km of the Guatemalan border between the Pacific Coast up to and including the border crossing at Gracias a Dio."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel on Federal Highway 199 (Carretera Federal 199) between Rancho Nuevo (just outside San Cristobal de las Casas) and the Chancalá junction just outside Palenque (where Federal Highway 199 meets Federal Highway 307)."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the city of Acapulco."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tijuana, except: airside transit through Tijuana airport the Cross Border Xpress bridge from the airport linking terminals across the Mexican-US border the federal toll road 1D and Via Rápida through Tijuana to the border FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tecate in Baja California, including roads between Tijuana and Tecate."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Chihuahua, except: the city of Chihuahua the border crossing in Ciudad Juárez (accessed by federal toll road 45) federal toll road 45D connecting the cities of Chihuahua and Ciudad Juárez the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Chihuahua and towns immediately on this route including Creel the road from Creel via San Juanito to San Pedro state highway 16 from San Pedro to Chihuahua There are high levels of organised crime activity, particularly human and drugs trafficking."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Sinaloa, except: the cities of Los Mochis and Mazatlán road 32 that runs between El Fuerte and Los Mochis the 15D federal toll road that runs the length of the state the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Los Mochis, El Fuerte and the towns immediately on this route Armed robbery and vehicle theft has happened in El Fuerte."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Tamaulipas, except: the border crossing at Nuevo Laredo accessed from Monterrey by federal toll road 85D – you should travel during daylight hours federal highways 80, 81 and 85 between Tampico, Ciudad de Victoria and Magueyes, and the entire area of Tamaulipas south of these highways Tamaulipas is dangerous due to the presence of many organised crime groups who fight for control of drug trafficking routes."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Zacatecas."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south-west of the road 45D."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Michoacán, except the: city of Morelia accessed by federal toll roads 15D, 126 and 43; and the federal toll road 48D between the city of Morelia and the General Francisco Mujica airport town of Pátzcuaro accessed by federal toll roads 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips out to islands on Lake Pátzcuaro federal highway 15D Michoacán is one of Mexico’s most violent states with high levels of organised crime and very little security presence."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the border state of Colima, specifically the municipalities of: Acatlán de Juárez Amacueca Ameca Atemajac de Brizuela Atengo Atenguillo Atoyac Autlán de Navarro Ayutla Casimiro Castillo Chiquilistlán Cocula Cuautitlán de García Barragán Cuautla Ejutla El Grullo El Limón Gómez Farias Guachinango Juchitlán Mixtlán San Gabriel San Marcos San Martín Hidalgo Sayula Tapalpa Techaluta de Montenegro Tecolotlán Tenamaxtlán Teocuitatlán de Corona Tolimán Tonaya Tuxcacuesco Tuxcueca Unión de Tula Villa Corona Villa Purificación Zacoalco de Torres Zapotitlán de Vadill Zapotlán el Grande FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the northern municipalities of: Bolaños Chimaltitán Colotlán Hostotipaquillo Huejúcar Huequilla el Alto Mezquitic San Martin de Bolaños Santa Maria de los Ángeles Totatiche Villa Guerrero This is due to inaccessibility for security forces, lack of state control, drugs cultivation and high levels of violence between rival criminal groups."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the whole state of Colima, except the city of Manzanillo accessed by sea or by air via Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport, and direct travel via road 200 from the airport to Manzanillo."}],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mexico","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-07-16T16:08:09+01:00"}},"timing":{"peak":"Dec-Apr (dry high season, northern-winter escape); event peak mid-May-mid-Sep whale sharks (peak Jul-Aug)","shoulder":"May, Jun, Sep (whale sharks present, rainy-season variability, softer rates)","green":"Oct (rainiest, many closures) + late Sep-Nov; November is the underrated value window","booking_window_lead_time":"3-6 months for Dec-Apr peak; tiny boutique inventory; book whale-shark tours ahead in event peak","out_of_season_fill_the_beds":"bioluminescence (new-moon year-round), Cabo Catoche/Isla Pasion boat tours, Yum Balam birding, kite season from Nov, boutique value rates","holiday_event_peaks":"Christmas-New Year, Semana Santa (Easter ~2x February rate), whale-shark peak Jul-Aug","campaign_start_trigger":"whale-shark campaigns Feb-Mar; dry-season/honeymoon campaigns Aug-Oct prior year; Nov green-window value late summer","flag":"whale-shark event peak OVERLAPS hurricane season (Jun-Nov, peak Aug-Oct) - sell with trip insurance + weather caveat","sources":["https://girlonazebra.com/best-time-to-visit-isla-holbox/","https://www.casasandra.com/blog/best-time-to-visit-holbox","https://puntacaliza.com/whale-sharks-in-holbox-best-season-and-tips-for-sightings/","https://www.islaholbox-info.com/en/holbox-island/travel-time-and-climate/"]},"jewels":[{"name":"Whale-shark snorkel aggregation","si_tag":"Global Expedition Adventures","status":"live","tier":"comfort","bookable":"CONANP-licensed full-day snorkel tour","source":"https://travelyucatan.com/whale-sharks-holbox/","hook":"swim beside the world''s largest fish in a controlled, no-touch encounter","si":"expedition","blurb":"swim beside the world''s largest fish in a controlled, no-touch encounter","commission":"local operator + Olympus/Amstar DMC + Viator affiliate"},{"name":"Punta Cocos bioluminescence night","si_tag":"Romance & Honeymoons","status":"live","tier":"essential","bookable":"guided bioluminescence tour","source":"https://sceneloc8.com/isla-holbox-a-car-free-paradise-of-beaches-and-bioluminescence/","timing":"Dec-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"plankton glow on the western tip on dark, moonless nights","si":"romance","blurb":"plankton glow on the western tip on dark, moonless nights","when":"Dec-Apr","commission":"local operator + Viator affiliate"},{"name":"Cabo Catoche / Isla Pasion three-islands boat tour","si_tag":"Ocean Adventures","status":"future","tier":"comfort","bookable":"boat/snorkel tour","source":"https://www.islaholbox-info.com/en/activities/tours-on-holbox/","timing":"Dec-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"ocean","when":"Dec-Apr","commission":"local operator + GYG affiliate"},{"name":"Yum Balam reserve birding + flamingos","si_tag":"Wildlife & Nature","status":"future","tier":"essential","bookable":"eco/kayak tour","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Isla_Holbox","hook":"~90% of Yucatán endemic birds; flamingos, crocodiles, in a protected mangrove reserve","si":"wildlife","blurb":"~90% of Yucatán endemic birds; flamingos, crocodiles, in a protected mangrove reserve","commission":"local operator + DMC"}],"faq":[{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for in Holbox?","a":"Open-water seasickness, mosquitoes and hurricane timing — not crime. Whale-shark boats run into open ocean where swells cause common seasickness (take motion meds 30–60 min before departure); this is a mangrove island so dengue is active (use repellent); and the whale-shark peak (Jul–Aug) overlaps hurricane season (Jun–Nov, peak Aug–Oct), so insure the trip.","source":"mexicowhaleshark.com / travel.state.gov, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"When and how can I swim with whale sharks in Holbox?","a":"Between May 15 and Sep 17, peaking July–August, on a full-day morning boat departure with a CONANP-licensed operator. The encounter is snorkel-only beside the world''s largest fish, with just two swimmers and a guide in the water at a time — book ahead during the event peak, as demand is high and operators are capped.","source":"travelyucatan.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"What is Holbox like as a car-free island?","a":"It is a barefoot sandbar with sand streets and no cars — you arrive by ferry from Chiquilá and move around by golf cart or moped. That car-free rhythm is the point: it is the slow, bohemian antidote to Cancún, built for beach days, bikes and sunsets rather than nightlife strips.","source":"en.wikipedia.org, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"tropical"},{"q":"Is Holbox good for a honeymoon?","a":"Yes, for couples who want quiet design over resort scale. There are no mass all-inclusives — just artist-owned boutiques like Ser Casasandra (17 rooms + 1 villa) and Punta Caliza (12 rooms) — plus bioluminescent night swims at Punta Cocos. Because inventory is tiny, book 3–6 months ahead for the Dec–Apr peak.","source":"casasandra.com / puntacaliza.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"What else is there to do in Holbox beyond whale sharks?","a":"Plenty year-round. Walk the bioluminescent shore at Punta Cocos on new-moon nights, take the Cabo Catoche / Isla Pasión \"three islands\" boat-and-snorkel tour, kayak the mangroves, or ride the kite-surf season that starts in November — the reasons to come when the whale sharks are gone.","source":"islaholbox-info.com / sceneloc8.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"ocean"},{"q":"What wildlife can I see in the Yum Balam reserve?","a":"A lot — Holbox sits inside the Yum Balam Flora & Fauna Protection Area, home to roughly 90% of the Yucatán''s endemic bird species, plus flamingos, crocodiles and turtles. Guided eco or kayak tours through the protected mangroves are the way to see them; birdlife is seasonal, so ask what''s present at your dates.","source":"en.wikipedia.org, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"wildlife"},{"q":"When is the best time to visit Holbox?","a":"December–April is the dry high season (blue skies, busiest); the whale-shark window is mid-May to mid-September. November is the underrated value pick — dry-season comfort, clean beaches and the start of kite season at low-season prices — while October is rainiest and many venues close. Easter rates run about double February.","source":"girlonazebra.com / islaholbox-info.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"planning"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Holbox Whale Sharks: Car-Free Island Guide","meta_description":"Snorkel with whale sharks off car-free Isla Holbox (mid-May–mid-Sep, no-touch, licensed operators) then walk a bioluminescent shore at Punta Cocos. When and how.","slug":"holbox-mexico","primary_keyword":"Holbox whale sharks","long_tail":["Holbox whale shark season 2026","Holbox bioluminescence Punta Cocos","car-free island Yucatan","Yum Balam biosphere Holbox","Holbox whale shark snorkel rules"],"search_language":["en","es-MX"],"local_keywords":["tiburón ballena Holbox","nadar con tiburón ballena Holbox temporada","isla sin autos Holbox","bioluminiscencia Punta Cocos","reserva Yum Balam Holbox","tours Holbox Cabo Catoche Isla Pasión","hoteles boutique Holbox"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","content_freshness":"2026-07-04"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"expedition","status":"live"},{"si":"romance","status":"live"},{"si":"ocean","status":"future"},{"si":"wildlife","status":"future"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Ser Casasandra","posture":"boutique-luxe (not branded ultra)","price_tier":"luxury","earning":"on application / host-Virtuoso or host-DMC block","direct_only":true,"mor":"commissionable only where offered; no net-rate resale","source":"https://www.casasandra.com/"},{"name":"Punta Caliza","posture":"boutique-luxe (12-room design boutique, not a chain)","price_tier":"luxury","earning":"on application / host-Virtuoso","direct_only":true,"mor":"no net-rate resale","source":"https://puntacaliza.com/whale-sharks-in-holbox-best-season-and-tips-for-sightings/"},{"name":"Villas HM Palapas del Mar","posture":"boutique-luxe (HM Hotels group, resort-shaped)","price_tier":"premier","earning":"on application; some bedbank/TAAP possible - verify terms","direct_only":false,"mor":"no net-rate resale","source":""},{"name":"Ser Casasandra luxury villa","posture":"closest to ultra buy-out on-island","price_tier":"ultra","earning":"on application / host-Virtuoso","direct_only":true,"mor":"no net-rate resale","source":"https://www.casasandra.com/"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-04","hero":{"query":"Holbox, Mexico"},"geo":{"lat":21.522,"lng":-87.379}}'::jsonb, 46),
  ('hopkins-belize', '10S', 'Hopkins', 'Belize', 'Garifuna drums and the southern reef', 'live', 'verified', 'tropicalBeach', 'Belize', '{"tropical","expedition","culture"}', '{"tropical"}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["The Garifuna cultural heart of Belize — living drumming tradition (Lebeha Drumming Center, est. 2002) and cuisine that is UNESCO-recognized intangible heritage (proclaimed 2001).","Gateway to Cockscomb Basin Wildlife Sanctuary — 128,000 acres, established 1986 as the world''s first jaguar preserve; ~200 jaguars and ~290 bird species.","One of the only places in Belize where the barrier reef and the rainforest are reachable from the same beach; South Water Caye is among the least-dived, healthiest reef systems in the country.","Mayflower Bocawina National Park (12 mi inland) has Belize''s longest zipline (2.5 mi) and its only guided waterfall rappel (Antelope Falls, 250 ft).","Garifuna Settlement Day (Nov 19) — Hopkins is one of three national epicenters, with a dawn Yurumein landing re-enactment and all-night drumming."],"safety":{"emergency":"911 (police & ambulance); maritime VHF Ch 16 or 966 — verify locally","hospital":"Dangriga (Southern Regional Hospital) for town care; serious trauma routes to Belize City; international medical evacuation the realistic path for major injury","recompression_chamber":"Ambergris Caye / San Pedro (24/7, tel 226-2660; DAN +1-919-648-9111) — FAR from Hopkins; dive conservatively","advisory_date":"2026-06-18","advisory_codes":"C (Crime) only","book_enabled":true,"consent_flow":{"bin":"BOOK WITH WARNING","disclosure_required":true,"renders":"full verbatim live US State Dept advisory for the country (level + reason + named-danger areas + complete ''If you decide to travel'' guidance), pulled live, plus traveler acknowledgment","wording_status":"hook set only — final consent language PENDING compliance-attorney sign-off"},"l3_disclosure":true,"state_dept_carveout":"only Southside Belize City restricted; Hopkins open","founder_policy_note":"book_enabled rides on TWW''s BOOK WITH WARNING (Four-Bin v3) posture — full-advisory disclosure + traveler acknowledgment at booking; only Southside Belize City is named, away from Hopkins","stay_in_zone":true,"air_access_verified":"BZE (Philip Goldson Intl) -> Dangriga/Hopkins DGA via Tropic Air/Maya Island Air (~25 min flight) + ~40 min drive; or ~2.5 hr direct drive from BZE","malaria":"WHO-certified malaria-free 2023; low localized inland risk only; dengue is an active 2026 risk (2,794 cases in 2025); jungle excursions raise mosquito exposure","water":"treat/bottled outside resorts"},"timing":{"peak_dry":"late-December to April","green_value_season":"June to November (30-40% savings)","event_peak":"Garifuna Settlement Day, November 19","secondary_events":["Hopkins Day (July)","Independence Day (September)"],"curve_start_dry":"mid-October","curve_start_event":"early-October","fire_date":"late-September to early-October","confidence":"seasonal-pattern-derived; sharpen on live booking pace"},"jewels":[{"name":"Lebeha Drumming Center","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lebeha_Drumming_Center","si":"culture","commission":"cultural experience add-on / direct-book"},{"name":"Warasa Garifuna Drum School (Punta Gorda)","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.warasadrumschool.com/","si":"culture","commission":"cultural add-on"},{"name":"Garifuna cuisine (hudut/sere/ereba) cooking class","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://belizenewspost.com/garifuna-food/","si":"culture","commission":"culinary experience / homestay bundle"},{"name":"Garifuna Settlement Day (Nov 19)","si_tag":"culture","tier":"comfort","source":"https://caribbeanlifestyle.com/garifuna-settlement-day-belize/","hook":"November 19 The single sharpest cultural spike of the year: dawn Yurumein re-enactment, all-night drumming, parades. Hopkins is one of three epicenters","si":"culture","blurb":"November 19 The single sharpest cultural spike of the year: dawn Yurumein re-enactment, all-night drumming, parades. Hopkins is one of three epicenters","commission":"event-anchored stay+culture package"},{"name":"Cockscomb Basin Wildlife Sanctuary (world''s first jaguar preserve)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cockscomb_Basin_Wildlife_Sanctuary","hook":"Established 1986, it holds ~200 jaguars plus puma, ocelot and ~290 bird species, reachable as a day trip rather than an expedition","si":"expedition","blurb":"Established 1986, it holds ~200 jaguars plus puma, ocelot and ~290 bird species, reachable as a day trip rather than an expedition","commission":"guided day-tour (gate non-commissionable)"},{"name":"Mayflower Bocawina National Park (waterfalls/zipline/rappel)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.islandexpeditions.com/belize-vacations-blog/5-ways-explore-mayflower-bocawina-national-park","si":"expedition","commission":"full-day adventure operator"},{"name":"Sittee River manatee & birding","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.magnumbelize.com/tours-2/sittee-river-kayaking/","hook":"Guided motorboat/kayak; crocodiles present — stay in the vessel, follow guide, no swimming in river sections. Manatees are protected — no-touch, no-chase","si":"expedition","blurb":"Guided motorboat/kayak; crocodiles present — stay in the vessel, follow guide, no swimming in river sections. Manatees are protected — no-touch, no-chase","commission":"half-day adventure operator"},{"name":"South Water Caye Marine Reserve + Glover''s Reef","si_tag":"tropical","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.zubludiving.com/destination/belize/stan-creek-district/hopkins-placencia-glovers-reef","si":"tropical","commission":"dive own CLIA lane; snorkel day-trip operators"}],"faq":[{"q":"What makes Hopkins different from Belize''s other beach spots?","a":"It is a rare double-header: one of the very few points on the Caribbean where the barrier reef and the rainforest are visible from the same beach chair, on a 12-mile beach. Because the southern barrier reef here fronts a low-population mainland, South Water Caye Marine Reserve is one of the least-dived, healthiest reef systems in the country.","source":"hamanasi.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"tropical"},{"q":"Can you visit the jaguar preserve from Hopkins?","a":"Yes — Cockscomb Basin, the world''s first jaguar preserve (128,000 acres, est. 1986), is about 30–40 minutes inland and works as a day trip, from an hour-long river stroll to a four-day Victoria Peak trek. The BZ$10 non-national entry fee is government pass-through; you book the guided day-tour for the value.","source":"hamanasi.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Is Hopkins a good honeymoon destination?","a":"Yes, for jungle-and-reef romance rather than resort glitz. Hamanasi — a Tripadvisor Top-25-in-world honoree with 30 treehouse/beachfront rooms, a PADI facility and Green Globe certification — plus Belizean Dreams and Jaguar Reef Lodge are built around couples with private-guide adventures and infinity pools.","source":"tripadvisor.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"Why is Hopkins the Garifuna cultural heart of Belize?","a":"Daily drum schools, homestays and food workshops make Hopkins the single most accessible stop to experience living Garifuna heritage — itself UNESCO-recognized intangible heritage (proclaimed 2001). Garifuna Settlement Day on November 19 brings a dawn Yurumein re-enactment and all-night drumming, and rooms in the village sell out.","source":"belizenewspost.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for in Hopkins?","a":"Medical remoteness and mosquitoes, not crime. The State Dept warns emergency medical services are \"usually unavailable or significantly delayed\" and serious cases \"normally require medical evacuation to another country,\" so evacuation-grade insurance is non-negotiable; the nearest hospital is Dangriga, with trauma routing to Belize City. Dengue is an active 2026 risk (2,794 cases in 2025), and jungle excursions raise exposure.","source":"travel.state.gov, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Is the Mayflower Bocawina waterfall rappel or the jungle hiking dangerous?","a":"Mayflower Bocawina holds Belize''s longest zipline (2.5 mi) and its only guided waterfall rappel (Antelope Falls, 250 ft) — certified guides and provided harness/helmet only, never solo. In Cockscomb, the Tiger Fern Trail now requires a guide (mandated after a hiker fatality) and Victoria Peak (3,675 ft) is dry-season-only and guide-mandatory.","source":"mayflowerbocawina.org, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Hopkins, Belize: Garifuna Culture, Jaguar Preserve & Reef Travel Guide (2026)","meta_description":"Hopkins is Belize''s Garifuna cultural heart — drumming, uncrowded beach, gateway to Cockscomb Basin jaguar preserve, Mayflower Bocawina waterfalls, and the southern barrier reef.","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","content_freshness":"2026-07-06","search_language":"en","local_keywords":["Hopkins Belize Garifuna drumming","Cockscomb Basin jaguar preserve tour from Hopkins","Hopkins Belize diving South Water Caye","Mayflower Bocawina waterfall rappel zipline","Sittee River manatee tour Belize","Garifuna Settlement Day Hopkins November 19","best time to visit Hopkins Belize","Hamanasi vs Belizean Dreams Hopkins","Hopkins Belize beach villa rental","is Hopkins Belize safe 2026","hudut Garifuna food Hopkins"],"hreflang":["en"]},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":["tropical","expedition","culture"],"ultra":[{"name":"Hamanasi Adventure & Dive Resort","location":"Hopkins","tier":"$$$$ premier","lane":"Fora/AOR · MoR","note":"Tripadvisor Top-25-in-world honoree; treehouses; Green Globe"},{"name":"Itz''ana Resort & Residences","location":"Placencia (~45-60 min south)","tier":"$$$$ ultra","lane":"Fora/AOR · MoR","note":"nearest true ultra; SLH / MICHELIN Guide; villas + marina"},{"name":"Naïa Resort & Spa","location":"Placencia","tier":"$$$$ ultra","lane":"Fora/AOR","note":"ultra beachfront spa/villa"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-06","hero":{"query":"Hopkins, Belize"},"geo":{"lat":16.105,"lng":-88.2867}}'::jsonb, 47)
