  ('huatulco-mexico', '10S', 'Huatulco', 'Mexico', 'Oaxaca''s calm nine-bay coast', 'live', 'verified', 'mountainValley', 'Oaxaca (Oaxaca City & Coast)', '{"expedition","diveglobal","ocean","culture","wildlife","wellness"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["Nine bays across 36 beaches; horseshoe coves stay calm for swimming/snorkeling — greener and calmer than surf-driven Puerto Escondido.","Huatulco National Park protects ~11,890 ha of coast, reef and forest; dolphins, turtles and seasonal whales.","Playa La Entrega is the best land-accessible snorkel cove — reef starts feet from shore.","Pluma Hidalgo (~1,350 m, 45 min inland) produces some of the Americas'' top high-altitude Arabica coffee.","Copalita is one of only two seaside archaeological sites in Mexico (with Tulum) — Zapotec/Mixtec city settled by ~500 BC.","Humpback whale season Dec 15-Mar 21 (97% sighting success at peak); olive-ridley/green turtle nesting Jul-Jan."],"safety":{"emergency":"911","hospital":"Local Huatulco/La Crucecita clinics stabilize routine cases; serious trauma routes to Oaxaca City or Mexico City for definitive/ICU care","advisory_level":"L2","advisory_note":"L2 (Oaxaca) — Exercise Increased Caution (Huatulco explicitly unrestricted); updated May 29, 2026","book_enabled":true,"bin":"freely bookable (L2)","consent_flow":false,"air_access_verified":true,"malaria":"low/negligible in Huatulco tourist coast","dengue":"endemic seasonal risk, higher May-Nov; use repellent","water":"bottled/purified only; resort water filtered","swimming":"calmer/safer bays than Puerto Escondido, but open beaches carry riptides — swim sheltered coves","hurricane_season":"Pacific storm season ~Jun-Oct; insure/refundable","fcdo":{"posture":"AREA-RESTRICTED","quotes":[{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel State of Baja California FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tijuana, except: airside transit through Tijuana airport the Cross Border Xpress bridge from the airport linking terminals across the Mexican-US border the federal toll road 1D and Via Rápida through Tijuana to the border FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tecate in Baja California, including roads between Tijuana and Tecate."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Chihuahua, except: the city of Chihuahua the border crossing in Ciudad Juárez (accessed by federal toll road 45) federal toll road 45D connecting the cities of Chihuahua and Ciudad Juárez the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Chihuahua and towns immediately on this route including Creel the road from Creel via San Juanito to San Pedro state highway 16 from San Pedro to Chihuahua State of Sinaloa FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Sinaloa, except: the cities of Los Mochis and Mazatlán road 32 that runs between El Fuerte and Los Mochis the 15D federal toll road that runs the length of the state the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Los Mochis, El Fuerte and the towns immediately on this route State of Tamaulipas FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Tamaulipas, except: the border crossing at Nuevo Laredo accessed by federal toll road 85D from Monterrey federal highways 80, 81 and 85 between Tampico, Ciudad de Victoria and Magueyes, and the entire area of Tamaulipas south of these highways State of Zacatecas FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Zacatecas."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south-west of road 45D."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Michoacán, except the: city of Morelia accessed by federal toll roads 15D, 126 and 43; and the federal toll road 48D between the city of Morelia and the General Francisco Mujica airport town of Pátzcuaro accessed by federal toll roads 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips out to islands on Lake Pátzcuaro Federal Highway 15D State of Jalisco FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the border with the state of Colima."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the northern municipalities of: Bolaños Chimaltitán Colotlán Hostotipaquillo Huejúcar Huequilla el Alto Mezquitic San Martin de Bolaños Santa Maria de los Ángeles Totatiche Villa Guerrero State of Colima FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Colima, except the city of Manzanillo accessed by sea or air via the Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport, and direct travel via road 200 from the airport to Manzanillo."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Guerrero, except the town of Zihuatanejo/Ixtapa accessed by air."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to within 40km of the Guatemalan border between the Pacific Coast up to and including the border crossing at Gracias a Dio."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel on Federal Highway 199 (Carretera Federal 199) between Rancho Nuevo (just outside San Cristobal de las Casas) and the Chancalá junction just outside Palenque (where Federal Highway 199 meets Federal Highway 307)."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the city of Acapulco."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tijuana, except: airside transit through Tijuana airport the Cross Border Xpress bridge from the airport linking terminals across the Mexican-US border the federal toll road 1D and Via Rápida through Tijuana to the border FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tecate in Baja California, including roads between Tijuana and Tecate."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Chihuahua, except: the city of Chihuahua the border crossing in Ciudad Juárez (accessed by federal toll road 45) federal toll road 45D connecting the cities of Chihuahua and Ciudad Juárez the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Chihuahua and towns immediately on this route including Creel the road from Creel via San Juanito to San Pedro state highway 16 from San Pedro to Chihuahua There are high levels of organised crime activity, particularly human and drugs trafficking."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Sinaloa, except: the cities of Los Mochis and Mazatlán road 32 that runs between El Fuerte and Los Mochis the 15D federal toll road that runs the length of the state the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Los Mochis, El Fuerte and the towns immediately on this route Armed robbery and vehicle theft has happened in El Fuerte."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Tamaulipas, except: the border crossing at Nuevo Laredo accessed from Monterrey by federal toll road 85D – you should travel during daylight hours federal highways 80, 81 and 85 between Tampico, Ciudad de Victoria and Magueyes, and the entire area of Tamaulipas south of these highways Tamaulipas is dangerous due to the presence of many organised crime groups who fight for control of drug trafficking routes."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Zacatecas."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south-west of the road 45D."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Michoacán, except the: city of Morelia accessed by federal toll roads 15D, 126 and 43; and the federal toll road 48D between the city of Morelia and the General Francisco Mujica airport town of Pátzcuaro accessed by federal toll roads 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips out to islands on Lake Pátzcuaro federal highway 15D Michoacán is one of Mexico’s most violent states with high levels of organised crime and very little security presence."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the border state of Colima, specifically the municipalities of: Acatlán de Juárez Amacueca Ameca Atemajac de Brizuela Atengo Atenguillo Atoyac Autlán de Navarro Ayutla Casimiro Castillo Chiquilistlán Cocula Cuautitlán de García Barragán Cuautla Ejutla El Grullo El Limón Gómez Farias Guachinango Juchitlán Mixtlán San Gabriel San Marcos San Martín Hidalgo Sayula Tapalpa Techaluta de Montenegro Tecolotlán Tenamaxtlán Teocuitatlán de Corona Tolimán Tonaya Tuxcacuesco Tuxcueca Unión de Tula Villa Corona Villa Purificación Zacoalco de Torres Zapotitlán de Vadill Zapotlán el Grande FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the northern municipalities of: Bolaños Chimaltitán Colotlán Hostotipaquillo Huejúcar Huequilla el Alto Mezquitic San Martin de Bolaños Santa Maria de los Ángeles Totatiche Villa Guerrero This is due to inaccessibility for security forces, lack of state control, drugs cultivation and high levels of violence between rival criminal groups."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the whole state of Colima, except the city of Manzanillo accessed by sea or by air via Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport, and direct travel via road 200 from the airport to Manzanillo."}],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mexico","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-07-16T16:08:09+01:00"}},"timing":{"peak":"Nov-Apr (dry season; sunny, no rain, highs 29-34C; whale window Dec-Mar)","inflection":"late Nov & April (shoulder value, still dry/sunny)","green":"May-Oct (rainy/low; hotter, lush, cheapest; overlaps turtle nesting)","whale_season":"humpbacks Dec 15-Mar 21, 97% sighting success at peak","turtle_season":"olive-ridley/green nesting Jul-Jan; hatchling-release draw","fire_date":"early-to-mid November — 1-2 weeks ahead of the Dec 15 humpback curve-start / dry-season flip","holiday_event_peaks":["Christmas/New Year","Semana Santa","whale-watch Dec-Mar"],"fill_the_beds":"green months lead with Pluma Hidalgo coffee day, Copalita eco-archaeology + river rafting, turtle-release evenings, calm-bay snorkel, green-season all-inclusive value","campaign_start_trigger":"open peak/whale campaigns early-mid Nov; shoulder (late Nov, Apr) ~3-4 months out; turtle-nesting green-season value push Jul-Oct"},"jewels":[{"name":"Nine-Bays boat tour","si_tag":"Ocean Adventures","status":"live","tier":"essential","hook":"Full-day boat expedition across the nine bays with beach + snorkel stops.","bookable_category":"guided boat tour","source":"https://www.amstardmc.com/en/excursions/sea-and-sun-bays/","si":"ocean","blurb":"Full-day boat expedition across the nine bays with beach + snorkel stops.","commission":"Amstar DMC ~12% / affiliate 4-8%; park bracelet pass-through"},{"name":"Bahia Maguey & Bahia Organo snorkel","si_tag":"Ocean Adventures","status":"future","tier":"essential","hook":"Calm-cove snorkel over close reef with beachfront seafood palapas at Maguey.","bookable_category":"boat snorkel stop","source":"https://www.viator.com/tours/Huatulco/Huatulco-National-Park-Sightseeing-Cruise-with-Snorkeling-in-Maguey-Bay/d4334-5885HUXSUN","si":"ocean","blurb":"Calm-cove snorkel over close reef with beachfront seafood palapas at Maguey.","commission":"affiliate / DMC ~12%; food pass-through"},{"name":"Playa La Entrega reef","si_tag":"Ocean Adventures","status":"future","tier":"essential","hook":"Land-accessible horseshoe cove — reef starts feet from shore, calm and current-sheltered.","bookable_category":"shore snorkel / rental","source":"https://mrplayas.com/blog/huatulco-oaxaca-guide","timing":"Nov-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"ocean","blurb":"Land-accessible horseshoe cove — reef starts feet from shore, calm and current-sheltered.","when":"Nov-Apr","commission":"affiliate 4-8% on packaged tours; DIY non-commissionable"},{"name":"Whale & dolphin watch","si_tag":"Wildlife & Nature","status":"future","tier":"comfort","hook":"Humpbacks Dec 15-Mar 21 (97% success at peak); year-round dolphins/turtles.","bookable_category":"wildlife boat safari","source":"https://seasafarihuatulco.com/whale-watching-tours/","si":"wildlife","blurb":"Humpbacks Dec 15-Mar 21 (97% success at peak); year-round dolphins/turtles.","commission":"operator affiliate / DMC ~12%"},{"name":"Cacaluta & San Agustin remote bays","si_tag":"Ocean Adventures","status":"future","tier":"comfort","hook":"Wild, undeveloped bays — heart-shaped Cacaluta and gin-clear San Agustin (18 m viz).","bookable_category":"private boat / dedicated tour","source":"https://www.tripadvisor.com/Attraction_Review-g150789-d524145-Reviews-Bahia_de_Cacaluta-Huatulco_Southern_Mexico.html","timing":"Nov-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"ocean","blurb":"Wild, undeveloped bays — heart-shaped Cacaluta and gin-clear San Agustin (18 m viz).","when":"Nov-Apr","commission":"DMC / operator affiliate; park bracelet pass-through"},{"name":"La Entrega / San Agustin reef dive","si_tag":"Dive Globally","status":"future","tier":"comfort","hook":"Beginner-to-intermediate protected-reef dives; San Agustin ~30 m sunken ship.","bookable_category":"reef dive (PADI operator)","source":"https://www.explorehuatulco.com/Huatulco-Scuba-Diving-Guide","timing":"Nov-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"diveglobal","blurb":"Beginner-to-intermediate protected-reef dives; San Agustin ~30 m sunken ship.","when":"Nov-Apr","commission":"dive-operator affiliate / DMC ~12%"},{"name":"Pluma Hidalgo coffee-finca day","si_tag":"Wellness","status":"future","tier":"comfort","hook":"45-min drive to ~1,350 m coffee country — finca tour, roasting, tasting, mirador views.","bookable_category":"guided coffee tour","source":"https://www.getyourguide.com/huatulco-l781/huatulco-santa-maria-and-pluma-hidalgo-coffee-tour-t631983/","timing":"Nov-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"wellness","blurb":"45-min drive to ~1,350 m coffee country — finca tour, roasting, tasting, mirador views.","when":"Nov-Apr","commission":"affiliate 4-8% / DMC ~12%"},{"name":"Copalita eco-archaeological park","si_tag":"Culture & Heritage","status":"future","tier":"essential","hook":"One of only two seaside archaeological sites in Mexico — Zapotec/Mixtec city in rainforest above the river mouth.","bookable_category":"guided park visit / combo","source":"https://lugares.inah.gob.mx/en/node/4487","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"culture","blurb":"One of only two seaside archaeological sites in Mexico — Zapotec/Mixtec city in rainforest above the river mouth.","when":"year-round","commission":"affiliate 4-8% / DMC ~12%; park entry pass-through"},{"name":"La Crucecita zocalo + Church of Guadalupe","si_tag":"Culture & Heritage","status":"future","tier":"essential","hook":"Real Oaxacan town with a zocalo, market, and one of Mexico''s largest Guadalupe ceiling murals.","bookable_category":"walking tour / DIY","source":"https://www.explorehuatulco.com/la-crucecita-region-huatulco-mexico","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"culture","blurb":"Real Oaxacan town with a zocalo, market, and one of Mexico''s largest Guadalupe ceiling murals.","when":"year-round","commission":"affiliate on guided walks; DIY non-commissionable"},{"name":"Copalita River rafting","si_tag":"Global Expedition Adventures","status":"live","tier":"comfort","hook":"Guided whitewater at La Bocana beside the archaeological site; fuller in green months.","bookable_category":"guided rafting","source":"https://www.huatulcowatersports.com/tours/copalita-archaological-site-143783","timing":"Nov-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"expedition","blurb":"Guided whitewater at La Bocana beside the archaeological site; fuller in green months.","when":"Nov-Apr","commission":"operator affiliate / DMC ~12%"}],"faq":[{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for in the water?","a":"Riptides on the open beaches, not the sheltered bays. The horseshoe coves (La Entrega, Maguey, San Agustín) are genuinely calm and swimmable, but open stretches of Tangolunda and Chahué carry rip currents — swim only the flagged, sheltered coves, and heed the flags.","source":"mrplayas.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Which bays are calm enough for swimming and families?","a":"The horseshoe coves. La Entrega is the best land-accessible snorkel cove — the reef starts feet from shore — and Maguey, Órgano and San Agustín stay calm inside their coves; that''s the difference from surf-driven Puerto Escondido up the coast.","source":"mrplayas.com / secretflying.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"tropical"},{"q":"What''s the one must-do day here?","a":"The nine-bays boat tour — a full-day (~7 h) expedition across the nine bays with beach and snorkel stops, bookable through Amstar''s \"Sea and Sun\"/\"Seven Bays\" excursions or affiliate marketplaces (the National Park conservation bracelet is a cash pass-through).","source":"amstardmc.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"When can I see whales?","a":"Humpbacks run **Dec 15–Mar 21**, with sightings on **over 97% of tours** at the peak, on boat safaris out of Santa Cruz; dolphins and turtles are year-round, and turtle nesting (olive-ridley/green) runs Jul–Jan.","source":"oceanico.org, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"wildlife"},{"q":"Can beginners dive the reef here?","a":"Yes — the protected Pacific reef is beginner-friendly. La Entrega runs 10–12 m and San Agustín adds a ~30 m sunken ship for advanced divers, with up to ~18 m visibility in the dry season; book only PADI-certified operators (Huatulco Dive Center, Anfibios, Hurricane Divers).","source":"explorehuatulco.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"diveglobal"},{"q":"Is there culture beyond the beach?","a":"Yes — Copalita is one of only two seaside archaeological sites in Mexico (with Tulum), a Zapotec/Mixtec city settled by ~500 BC in rainforest above the river mouth, and La Crucecita''s zócalo holds one of Mexico''s largest Guadalupe ceiling murals.","source":"lugares.inah.gob.mx, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"Is Huatulco good for a honeymoon?","a":"Yes, for calm-bay romance rather than branded-ultra. Secrets Huatulco is the adults-only, all-oceanfront-suite anchor of the Tangolunda strip; the coast tops out at premier all-inclusive plus a top oceanfront villa in Conejos — there is no Aman/Rosewood-tier hotel here.","source":"hyattinclusivecollection.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"romance"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Huatulco Travel Guide 2026 — Nine Bays, Snorkel & Coffee Country | TravelWell.World","meta_description":"Plan Huatulco, Oaxaca''s calm eco-resort coast: the nine-bays boat tour, Maguey/Organo snorkel, La Crucecita, Pluma Hidalgo coffee, Copalita eco-archaeology, whale season, Level 2 safety (Huatulco unrestricted).","slug":"huatulco-mexico","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","content_freshness":"2026-07-07","search_language":"es-MX","local_keywords":["qué hacer en Huatulco","Bahías de Huatulco","La Crucecita","tour de las nueve bahías Huatulco","snorkel en Bahía Maguey","café Pluma Hidalgo tour","Parque Eco-Arqueológico Copalita","avistamiento de ballenas Huatulco","mejor época para visitar Huatulco","buceo en Huatulco","villas frente al mar Conejos Huatulco"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"]},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"expedition","status":"live"},{"si":"diveglobal","status":"future"},{"si":"ocean","status":"future"},{"si":"culture","status":"future"},{"si":"wildlife","status":"future"},{"si":"wellness","status":"future"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Secrets Huatulco Resort & Spa","price_tier":"premier","virtuoso":false,"earning":"all-incl -> OA host AOR + Hyatt Inclusive TA ~12%","mor_posture":true,"note":"adults-only all-oceanfront-suite; the branded ceiling for the coast","source":"https://www.hyattinclusivecollection.com/en/resorts-hotels/secrets/mexico/huatulco-resort-spa/"},{"name":"Dreams Huatulco Resort & Spa","price_tier":"comfort-premier","virtuoso":false,"earning":"OA host AOR + Hyatt Inclusive TA ~12%","mor_posture":true,"note":"family sister with shared Secrets access","source":"https://www.tripadvisor.com/Hotel_Review-g150789-d2089597-Reviews-Secrets_Huatulco_Resort_Spa-Huatulco_Southern_Mexico.html"},{"name":"Las Palmas Resort","price_tier":"comfort","virtuoso":false,"earning":"OA host AOR","mor_posture":true,"source":"https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowTopic-g150789-i740-k14655958-Secrets_vs_Dreams_vs_Barcelo-Huatulco_Southern_Mexico.html"},{"name":"Boutique bay villas — Residencial Conejos (oceanfront)","price_tier":"ultra","virtuoso":false,"earning":"on application / via host or DMC villa AOR","mor_posture":true,"note":"villa ceiling; no branded true-ultra hotel on this eco-resort coast; net-rate resale red","source":"https://www.airbnb.com/santa-maria-huatulco-mexico/stays/villas"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-07","hero":{"query":"Huatulco, Mexico"},"geo":{"lat":15.76,"lng":-96.13}}'::jsonb, 48),
  ('iguazu-falls-argentina', '10S', 'Iguazú Falls (Argentine Side)', 'Argentina', 'Iguazú Falls (Argentine Side)', 'live', 'verified', 'mountainValley', 'Northwest, Mendoza Wine & Iguazú', '{"expedition","culture"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","luxury","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":null,"safety":{"emergency":"911","emergency_secondary":["101 police","107 ambulance (SAME)","100 fire","0800 999 5000 tourist line"],"advisory_level":"L1","book_enabled":true,"bin":"freely bookable (L1)","consent_flow":false,"air_access_verified":true,"air_access_note":"Puerto Iguazu / Cataratas del Iguazu Intl (IGR) via Buenos Aires AEP (domestic) / EZE (international); daily nonstops on Aerolineas Argentinas / Flybondi / JetSmart; IGR<->AEP among busiest domestic routes","trauma_note":"Puerto Iguazu hospital stabilises; serious trauma evac to Buenos Aires by air (IGR->AEP/EZE)","falls_footing":"catwalks + circuit boardwalks/stairs permanently misted & slippery; Lower Circuit most stair-heavy; Throat catwalk can close on river surge","gran_aventura_boat":"mandatory life jacket + briefing + dry-bags; jacket-quality reviews mixed; total soaking; river-level-dependent","triple_frontier_note":"Argentina-Brazil-Paraguay convergence is a transnational-crime region; avoid the Paraguay/Ciudad del Este side casually; park + Puerto Iguazu core safe with standard precautions; cross to Brazil before nightfall","health":"Misiones = CDC yellow-fever recommended + dengue risk; DEET, dawn/dusk cover, pre-travel vaccination consult","wildlife":"coatis bold near viewpoints — do NOT feed (bite/scratch)","mandatory_insurance":"Non-resident travel medical insurance required since 2025-07-01 (hospitalisation, repatriation, evacuation)","fcdo":{"posture":"1","quotes":[],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/argentina","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-05-07T17:26:11+01:00"}},"timing":{"peak_experience":"Mar-Apr & Aug-Sep (best flow-weather-crowd balance)","peak_flow_and_crowds":"Dec-Feb (max water flow, heat >35C, peak crowds); Easter week (Apr) crowd spike","shoulder_sleeper":"May (autumn flow, 30-40% lower rates)","quietest_days":"Tue-Thu","full_moon_walk":"5 nights/month only — plan around lunar calendar; 3 nightly departures, ~2.5 hr","fire_date":"curve-start minus 1-2 weeks; ~2 weeks before visible curve for a standard trip, but 6-12 months ahead for Awasi Iguazu or an in-park Gran Melia falls-view room"},"jewels":[{"name":"Garganta del Diablo catwalk (Devil''s Throat)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://iguazufalls-tickets.org/what-to-see/devils-throat-iguazu-falls/","hook":"the marquee: 1.1 km of steel walkway out over the U-shaped canyon where 14 falls drop 82 m into permanent mist","si":"expedition","blurb":"the marquee: 1.1 km of steel walkway out over the U-shaped canyon where 14 falls drop 82 m into permanent mist","commission":"park-fee entry (non-commissionable) + DMC land package / activity affiliate framing"},{"name":"Upper Circuit","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://iguazufalls.com/travel-guide/the-circuits-in-iguazu-falls/","hook":"~1.75 km, mostly flat, top-down panoramas across the cataract chain; the accessible headline alongside the Throat catwalk","si":"expedition","blurb":"~1.75 km, mostly flat, top-down panoramas across the cataract chain; the accessible headline alongside the Throat catwalk","commission":"park-fee + DMC/affiliate"},{"name":"Lower Circuit + Isla San Martín boat","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://iguazutickets.com/guides/what-to-see-at-iguazu-falls/","hook":"~1.7 km, stairs down to the base, closest in-your-face angle, plus the passenger boat to the rocky Isla San Martín and its beach","si":"expedition","blurb":"~1.7 km, stairs down to the base, closest in-your-face angle, plus the passenger boat to the rocky Isla San Martín and its beach","commission":"park-fee + DMC/affiliate"},{"name":"Gran Aventura — under-the-falls boat + 4x4","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","source":"https://iguazufalls.com/tours-and-activities/gran-aventura-activity/","hook":"the adrenaline jewel: 4×4 jungle trail to Puerto Macuco, then a 6 km semi-rigid run into the San Martín falls \"baptism of the mists.\"","si":"expedition","blurb":"the adrenaline jewel: 4×4 jungle trail to Puerto Macuco, then a 6 km semi-rigid run into the San Martín falls \"baptism of the mists.\"","commission":"in-park concession (largely non-commissionable) — package via DMC / frame via activity affiliate"},{"name":"Full-Moon Walk (Paseos de Luna Llena)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","source":"https://iguazufalls.com/tours-and-activities/full-moon-walk-tour/","hook":"5 nights a month only, timed to the full moon: welcome drink + Guaraní music, Eco-Train through the night jungle to the Throat catwalk","si":"expedition","blurb":"5 nights a month only, timed to the full moon: welcome drink + Guaraní music, Eco-Train through the night jungle to the Throat catwalk","commission":"guided-only ticket via activity affiliate + DMC"},{"name":"Sunrise with in-park hotel (Gran Meliá privilege)","si_tag":"GEA/RHN","tier":"ultra","source":"https://www.jacadatravel.com/latin-america/argentina/iguazu-falls/accommodation/melia-iguazu/","si":"GEA/RHN","commission":"in-park hotel booking (ultra lane)"},{"name":"Macuco jungle trail","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"http://www.iguazujungle.com/eng/web2/","hook":"the park''s longer forest walk to a hidden waterfall; coatis, toucans, capuchins, butterflies","si":"expedition","blurb":"the park''s longer forest walk to a hidden waterfall; coatis, toucans, capuchins, butterflies","commission":"self-guided or guided via in-park operator + DMC"},{"name":"Güirá Oga wildlife refuge","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.welcomeargentina.com/puertoiguazu/lodge-awasi-iguazu_i.html","hook":"\"bird house\" in Guaraní; a rescue-and-rehab centre for trafficked/injured native fauna just outside Puerto Iguazú","si":"expedition","blurb":"\"bird house\" in Guaraní; a rescue-and-rehab centre for trafficked/injured native fauna just outside Puerto Iguazú","commission":"activity affiliate + DMC add-on"},{"name":"Brazilian-side panorama day-trip","si_tag":"culture","tier":"comfort","source":"https://sayhueque.com/our-trips/iguazu-falls/","hook":"cross to Parque Nacional do Iguaçu for the whole-system framed view Argentina can''t give you; passport-required border crossing, ~3–4 hr","si":"culture","blurb":"cross to Parque Nacional do Iguaçu for the whole-system framed view Argentina can''t give you; passport-required border crossing, ~3–4 hr","commission":"DMC/guided transfer + activity affiliate (cross-ref Brazil-side dossier)"},{"name":"San Ignacio Miní (UNESCO Jesuit-Guaraní mission)","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://whc.unesco.org/en/list/275/","hook":"the roofless red-sandstone cathedral of a 1610 Jesuit reduction, UNESCO-listed 1984, ~300 km south toward Posadas","si":"culture","blurb":"the roofless red-sandstone cathedral of a 1610 Jesuit reduction, UNESCO-listed 1984, ~300 km south toward Posadas","commission":"DMC / guided excursion + activity affiliate"}],"faq":[{"q":"What''s the best plan for a day at Iguazú Falls?","a":"Run the Devil''s Throat first at the 08:00 park opening, then work back through the Upper and Lower Circuits. The park opens 08:00 and closes 18:00 with last falls access around 16:30, and starting at the Garganta station gives the best rainbow light and thinnest crowds; budget 5–6 hours minimum for all three circuits plus the Eco-Train.","source":"iguazufalls-tickets.org, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"When is the best time to visit Iguazú Falls?","a":"March–April and August–September are the sweet spot, because they balance strong water flow with comfortable 20–30 °C temperatures and manageable crowds. December–February brings maximum flow but heat above 35 °C and peak crowds, while May is a quiet sleeper month with autumn flow and room rates 30–40% below the Dec–Feb peak.","source":"iguazutickets.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Where should honeymooners stay at Iguazú?","a":"The two scarce in-jewel beds are the play: Awasi Iguazú (Relais & Châteaux, 14 stilted villas with a private guide and 4×4 each) and the Gran Meliá Iguazú, the only hotel inside the Argentine park. Both are near-zero on bedbanks and contract direct or via DMC, so book Awasi or an in-park falls-view room 6–12 months ahead.","source":"relaischateaux.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"Should I visit the Brazilian side too — and what else is nearby?","a":"Yes if time allows: Argentina holds ~80% of the falls and the immersion, while Brazil''s single panoramic boardwalk delivers the whole-system view as a passport-required border day-trip. South toward Posadas, the roofless red-sandstone cathedral of San Ignacio Miní (UNESCO-listed 1984) rounds out a cultural-heritage circuit.","source":"sayhueque.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for at Iguazú?","a":"Health and weather, not crime. Misiones province carries a CDC yellow-fever vaccination recommendation and a real dengue risk, so pack DEET and get a pre-travel vaccination consult; the catwalks are permanently misted and slippery, and extreme rainfall can close the Devil''s Throat catwalk on river surge.","source":"wwwnc.cdc.gov, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Is the Gran Aventura speedboat dangerous?","a":"It is operator-run and low-risk with the rules followed, but not trivial. A life jacket is mandatory and a safety briefing is given before the 6 km run into the San Martín falls; jacket-quality reviews are mixed, so non-swimmers should weigh the run, everyone gets thoroughly soaked, and the trip is river-level-dependent and cancels in high water.","source":"iguazufalls.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Iguazú Falls, Argentine Side: Devil''s Throat, the Circuits & Gran Aventura Boat | TravelWell.World","meta_description":"Stand over the Devil''s Throat, walk the Upper and Lower Circuits, run the Gran Aventura boat under the falls, and stay inside the national park — the complete guide to the Argentine side of Iguazú.","long_tail_en":["iguazu falls argentine side guide","garganta del diablo devil''s throat iguazu","iguazu upper and lower circuits","gran aventura boat ride iguazu","iguazu falls full moon walk","best time to visit iguazu falls","gran melia iguazu in-park hotel","awasi iguazu relais chateaux","iguazu argentina vs brazil side","san ignacio mini jesuit ruins"],"search_language":"es-AR","local_keywords":["Cataratas del Iguazú","Garganta del Diablo","Gran Aventura Iguazú","circuito superior e inferior Iguazú","Tren Ecológico de la Selva","paseo de luna llena Cataratas","San Ignacio Miní ruinas","qué hacer en Puerto Iguazú"],"hreflang":["en","es-AR"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","freshness":"2026-07-07","primary_keyword":"Iguazú Falls (Argentine Side)"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"expedition","status":"live"},{"si":"culture","status":"live"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Awasi Iguazu","type":"Relais & Chateaux all-inclusive villa lodge","location":"Misiones jungle, ~20 min from falls","earning":"Virtuoso/Fora advisor commission + amenities","mor":"AOR/advisor","tier":"ultra"},{"name":"Gran Melia Iguazu","type":"in-park hotel (only one, Argentine side)","location":"inside Iguazu National Park","earning":"advisor/DMC commission + RedLevel upsell","mor":"AOR/advisor/DMC","tier":"ultra"},{"name":"Loi Suites Iguazu","type":"upscale jungle-river resort","location":"Iryapu reserve, ~10 min from Puerto Iguazu","earning":"advisor/DMC commission","mor":"AOR/DMC","tier":"luxury"}],"source_verified":null,"hero":{"query":"Iguazú Falls (Argentine Side), Argentina"},"geo":{"lat":-25.6953,"lng":-54.4367}}'::jsonb, 49),
