ises against all but essential travel to the state of Sinaloa, except: the cities of Los Mochis and Mazatlán road 32 that runs between El Fuerte and Los Mochis the 15D federal toll road that runs the length of the state the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Los Mochis, El Fuerte and the towns immediately on this route State of Tamaulipas FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Tamaulipas, except: the border crossing at Nuevo Laredo accessed by federal toll road 85D from Monterrey federal highways 80, 81 and 85 between Tampico, Ciudad de Victoria and Magueyes, and the entire area of Tamaulipas south of these highways State of Zacatecas FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Zacatecas."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south-west of road 45D."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Michoacán, except the: city of Morelia accessed by federal toll roads 15D, 126 and 43; and the federal toll road 48D between the city of Morelia and the General Francisco Mujica airport town of Pátzcuaro accessed by federal toll roads 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips out to islands on Lake Pátzcuaro Federal Highway 15D State of Jalisco FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the border with the state of Colima."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the northern municipalities of: Bolaños Chimaltitán Colotlán Hostotipaquillo Huejúcar Huequilla el Alto Mezquitic San Martin de Bolaños Santa Maria de los Ángeles Totatiche Villa Guerrero State of Colima FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Colima, except the city of Manzanillo accessed by sea or air via the Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport, and direct travel via road 200 from the airport to Manzanillo."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Guerrero, except the town of Zihuatanejo/Ixtapa accessed by air."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to within 40km of the Guatemalan border between the Pacific Coast up to and including the border crossing at Gracias a Dio."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel on Federal Highway 199 (Carretera Federal 199) between Rancho Nuevo (just outside San Cristobal de las Casas) and the Chancalá junction just outside Palenque (where Federal Highway 199 meets Federal Highway 307)."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the city of Acapulco."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tijuana, except: airside transit through Tijuana airport the Cross Border Xpress bridge from the airport linking terminals across the Mexican-US border the federal toll road 1D and Via Rápida through Tijuana to the border FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tecate in Baja California, including roads between Tijuana and Tecate."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Chihuahua, except: the city of Chihuahua the border crossing in Ciudad Juárez (accessed by federal toll road 45) federal toll road 45D connecting the cities of Chihuahua and Ciudad Juárez the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Chihuahua and towns immediately on this route including Creel the road from Creel via San Juanito to San Pedro state highway 16 from San Pedro to Chihuahua There are high levels of organised crime activity, particularly human and drugs trafficking."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Sinaloa, except: the cities of Los Mochis and Mazatlán road 32 that runs between El Fuerte and Los Mochis the 15D federal toll road that runs the length of the state the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Los Mochis, El Fuerte and the towns immediately on this route Armed robbery and vehicle theft has happened in El Fuerte."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Tamaulipas, except: the border crossing at Nuevo Laredo accessed from Monterrey by federal toll road 85D – you should travel during daylight hours federal highways 80, 81 and 85 between Tampico, Ciudad de Victoria and Magueyes, and the entire area of Tamaulipas south of these highways Tamaulipas is dangerous due to the presence of many organised crime groups who fight for control of drug trafficking routes."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Zacatecas."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south-west of the road 45D."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Michoacán, except the: city of Morelia accessed by federal toll roads 15D, 126 and 43; and the federal toll road 48D between the city of Morelia and the General Francisco Mujica airport town of Pátzcuaro accessed by federal toll roads 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips out to islands on Lake Pátzcuaro federal highway 15D Michoacán is one of Mexico’s most violent states with high levels of organised crime and very little security presence."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the border state of Colima, specifically the municipalities of: Acatlán de Juárez Amacueca Ameca Atemajac de Brizuela Atengo Atenguillo Atoyac Autlán de Navarro Ayutla Casimiro Castillo Chiquilistlán Cocula Cuautitlán de García Barragán Cuautla Ejutla El Grullo El Limón Gómez Farias Guachinango Juchitlán Mixtlán San Gabriel San Marcos San Martín Hidalgo Sayula Tapalpa Techaluta de Montenegro Tecolotlán Tenamaxtlán Teocuitatlán de Corona Tolimán Tonaya Tuxcacuesco Tuxcueca Unión de Tula Villa Corona Villa Purificación Zacoalco de Torres Zapotitlán de Vadill Zapotlán el Grande FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the northern municipalities of: Bolaños Chimaltitán Colotlán Hostotipaquillo Huejúcar Huequilla el Alto Mezquitic San Martin de Bolaños Santa Maria de los Ángeles Totatiche Villa Guerrero This is due to inaccessibility for security forces, lack of state control, drugs cultivation and high levels of violence between rival criminal groups."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the whole state of Colima, except the city of Manzanillo accessed by sea or by air via Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport, and direct travel via road 200 from the airport to Manzanillo."}],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mexico","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-07-16T16:08:09+01:00"}},"timing":{"peak":"Dec-Apr (dry, calm seas, best Ixlaché clarity) + Jun-Sep whale-shark corridor (sold as whale-shark + Contoy combos = true event peak)","shoulder":"May-Jun & Nov (easier permit-day availability; May-Jun straddles whale-shark open + turtle-nesting start)","green":"Jun-mid-Oct (hurricane season; exposed ~30 km open-water crossing - trips cancel in rough seas; disclose cancellation policy)","booking_lead":"200/day cap + authorized-only = book 3-6+ wks in peak (combos sell out with summer 30-39-day window), 1-3 wks shoulder; popular operators + calm-sea Sundays fill first","off_season_specials":"no beds - ''fill-the-permit-days'': green/shoulder = calm-day nature escape (birds + Ixlaché) bundled with off-island Isla Mujeres/Cancún stay","event_peaks":"Christmas-NY + spring break (Dec-Apr); sea-turtle nesting (May-Oct) + whale-shark run (Jun-Sep) are the island''s wildlife event peaks","campaign_start":"whale-shark + Contoy combo Mar-Apr (6-8 wks pre-open); dry-season Ixlaché day-trip Aug-Sep; always pair with off-island stay CTA"},"jewels":[{"name":"Contoy authorized eco-expedition (200/day cap)","si_tag":"Global Expedition Adventures","status":"live","tier":"comfort","hook":"permitted boat + guided trail through frigatebird/pelican colonies","bookable_category":"authorized eco day tour","source":"https://contoyadventures.com/isla-contoy/","timing":"Dec-Apr  + Jun-Sep whale-shark corridor","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"expedition","blurb":"permitted boat + guided trail through frigatebird/pelican colonies","when":"Dec-Apr  + Jun-Sep whale-shark corridor","commission":"authorized operator → DMC/curated (park fee pass-through)"},{"name":"Ixlaché reef snorkel","si_tag":"Ocean Adventures","status":"future","tier":"comfort","hook":"northern start of world''s 2nd-largest barrier reef, 17 hard + 14 soft corals","bookable_category":"snorkel stop within Contoy tour","source":"https://contoyadventures.com/isla-contoy/","timing":"Dec-Apr  + Jun-Sep whale-shark corridor","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"ocean","blurb":"northern start of world''s 2nd-largest barrier reef, 17 hard + 14 soft corals","when":"Dec-Apr  + Jun-Sep whale-shark corridor","commission":"authorized operator → curated (bundled)"},{"name":"173+ bird species + sea-turtle nesting","si_tag":"Wildlife & Nature","status":"future","tier":"comfort","hook":"frigatebirds, pelicans, green/loggerhead nesting beaches (May-Oct)","bookable_category":"guided nature walk (within tour)","source":"https://nationalparksassociation.org/mexico-national-parks/isla-contoy-national-park/","si":"wildlife","blurb":"frigatebirds, pelicans, green/loggerhead nesting beaches (May-Oct)","commission":"authorized operator → curated (conservation fee non-commissionable)"}],"faq":[{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for on an Isla Contoy trip?","a":"The open-water crossing and weather — not crime. Contoy sits ~30 km out at the seam where the Caribbean meets the Gulf, an exposed run where sea state can build and operators cancel trips in rough weather (especially hurricane season, Jun–Nov). Pick a calm-sea day, confirm the cancellation/reschedule policy, and keep life jackets on during transit.","source":"airial.travel, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Is the reef snorkel and boat crossing dangerous?","a":"Both are low-risk with a guide, but respect the water. Snorkeling is snorkel-only with no decompression restriction — the real hazards are the open-water current at the reef seam, boat traffic and sun, so wear the vest, avoid all coral/wildlife contact and stay with the guide. On the ~30 km crossing, follow crew instructions and keep life jackets on.","source":"nationalparksassociation.org, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"How do you actually visit Isla Contoy?","a":"Only through a handful of authorized operators — there is no independent access. The daily cap of 200 visitors makes it scarcity-priced, so book 3–6+ weeks ahead in peak season (1–3 weeks in shoulder); popular operators and calm-sea days fill first. Every trip bundles the park fee, lunch and snorkel gear.","source":"contoyadventures.com / airial.travel, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"What is the Ixlaché reef snorkel like?","a":"It is the headline in-water stop — the northern start of the world''s second-largest barrier reef. Ixlaché holds 17 hard and 14 soft coral species just south of the island; visibility is clearest in the dry season (Dec–Apr), and the snorkel is included in the guided tour on calm-sea days.","source":"contoyadventures.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"ocean"},{"q":"What wildlife will I see on Isla Contoy?","a":"Birds above all — the island is critical habitat for 173+ species, with frigatebird and pelican colonies you pass on the marked trails. Green and loggerhead sea turtles nest on the beaches May–October, adding a seasonal wildlife hook; the whole reserve is car-free and strictly protected.","source":"nationalparksassociation.org, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"wildlife"},{"q":"When is the best time to visit Isla Contoy, and where do trips leave from?","a":"December–April brings the calmest seas and clearest Ixlaché water; the summer whale-shark run (roughly Jun–Sep) is the true event peak, since Contoy is often sold as a whale-shark + Contoy combo. Trips depart Cancún and Isla Mujeres marinas on ~7–8 hour days — there is no lodging, so base off-island.","source":"isla-seatours.com / machupicchu.org, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"planning"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Isla Contoy, Mexico: 200-a-Day National Park Island","meta_description":"Uninhabited and capped at 200 visitors a day — Isla Contoy''s bird sanctuary and Ixlaché reef are authorized-tour-only. How to book the trip and what to expect.","slug":"isla-contoy-mexico","primary_keyword":"Isla Contoy national park tour","long_tail":["Isla Contoy 200 visitors per day","Ixlaché reef snorkeling","Isla Contoy bird sanctuary","Isla Contoy day trip from Cancún","Isla Contoy authorized operators"],"search_language":"es-MX (restated, not machine-translated)","local_keywords":["tour a Isla Contoy","Parque Nacional Isla Contoy","snorkel arrecife Ixlaché","santuario de aves Isla Contoy","excursión Isla Contoy desde Cancún","operadores autorizados Isla Contoy","combo tiburón ballena e Isla Contoy"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"],"jsonld_type":"TouristAttraction","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","content_freshness":"2026-07-04"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"expedition","status":"live"},{"si":"ocean","status":"future"},{"si":"wildlife","status":"future"}],"ultra":[{"name":"NONE - uninhabited national park, no lodging","why_ultra":"Isla Contoy is an uninhabited national park: no hotels/villas/lodging, no overnight permitted - day-trip add-on, not a stay. Ultra play lives off-island (Isla Mujeres Impression / Cancún Nizuc / Mayakoba corridor - verify municipality)","earning":"n/a on-island; on application via associated Isla Mujeres/Puerto Morelos dossiers","virtuoso_value_add":"n/a on-island - see associated dossiers","mor":"no on-island revenue; commission captured on associated stay + day-tour","source":"https://nationalparksassociation.org/mexico-national-parks/isla-contoy-national-park/"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-04","hero":{"query":"Isla Contoy, Mexico"},"geo":{"lat":21.4833,"lng":-86.7917}}'::jsonb, 50),
