avel to the state of Sinaloa, except: the cities of Los Mochis and Mazatlán road 32 that runs between El Fuerte and Los Mochis the 15D federal toll road that runs the length of the state the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Los Mochis, El Fuerte and the towns immediately on this route Armed robbery and vehicle theft has happened in El Fuerte."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Tamaulipas, except: the border crossing at Nuevo Laredo accessed from Monterrey by federal toll road 85D – you should travel during daylight hours federal highways 80, 81 and 85 between Tampico, Ciudad de Victoria and Magueyes, and the entire area of Tamaulipas south of these highways Tamaulipas is dangerous due to the presence of many organised crime groups who fight for control of drug trafficking routes."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Zacatecas."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south-west of the road 45D."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Michoacán, except the: city of Morelia accessed by federal toll roads 15D, 126 and 43; and the federal toll road 48D between the city of Morelia and the General Francisco Mujica airport town of Pátzcuaro accessed by federal toll roads 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips out to islands on Lake Pátzcuaro federal highway 15D Michoacán is one of Mexico’s most violent states with high levels of organised crime and very little security presence."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the border state of Colima, specifically the municipalities of: Acatlán de Juárez Amacueca Ameca Atemajac de Brizuela Atengo Atenguillo Atoyac Autlán de Navarro Ayutla Casimiro Castillo Chiquilistlán Cocula Cuautitlán de García Barragán Cuautla Ejutla El Grullo El Limón Gómez Farias Guachinango Juchitlán Mixtlán San Gabriel San Marcos San Martín Hidalgo Sayula Tapalpa Techaluta de Montenegro Tecolotlán Tenamaxtlán Teocuitatlán de Corona Tolimán Tonaya Tuxcacuesco Tuxcueca Unión de Tula Villa Corona Villa Purificación Zacoalco de Torres Zapotitlán de Vadill Zapotlán el Grande FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the northern municipalities of: Bolaños Chimaltitán Colotlán Hostotipaquillo Huejúcar Huequilla el Alto Mezquitic San Martin de Bolaños Santa Maria de los Ángeles Totatiche Villa Guerrero This is due to inaccessibility for security forces, lack of state control, drugs cultivation and high levels of violence between rival criminal groups."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the whole state of Colima, except the city of Manzanillo accessed by sea or by air via Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport, and direct travel via road 200 from the airport to Manzanillo."}],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mexico","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-07-16T16:08:09+01:00"}},"timing":{"peak":"Dec-Apr (region dry/high season) + Jun-Sep whale-shark event peak (snorkel-only)","shoulder":"May-Jun & Nov (~30-40% off winter rates)","green":"Jun-mid-Oct (hurricane season, ~40-60% off; whale-shark peak sits inside it)","booking_lead":"whale-shark tours ~30-39 days (book 3-6 wks ahead, sells out summer); shoulder beds 2-4 wks; ultra/boutique suites Dec-Apr + holidays 3-6+ months","off_season_specials":"green-season play = discounted island bed + premium whale-shark excursion (''cheap bed, peak wildlife''); disclose hurricane/sargassum","event_peaks":"Christmas-New Year, US spring break (Mar); whale-shark open (early Jun) + Jul-Aug midsummer height","campaign_start":"whale-shark Mar-Apr (6-8 wks pre-open); winter/honeymoon-suite Aug-Sep; green-season value Apr-May"},"jewels":[{"name":"Whale-shark snorkel departures","si_tag":"ocean","status":"future","tier":"comfort","hook":"island boats to the aggregation, Jun-Sept, snorkel-only","bookable_category":"boat snorkel excursion","source":"https://mexicodivers.com/","si":"ocean","blurb":"island boats to the aggregation, Jun-Sept, snorkel-only","commission":"DMC/local operator → OTA affiliate"},{"name":"MUSA south wing","si_tag":"diveglobal","status":"future","tier":"comfort","hook":"shallow sculpture reef divable by beginners and snorkelers","bookable_category":"dive/snorkel tour","source":"https://www.bluewaterdivetravel.com/scuba-musa-isla-mujeres-cancun","timing":"Dec-Apr  + Jun-Sep whale-shark event peak","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"diveglobal","blurb":"shallow sculpture reef divable by beginners and snorkelers","when":"Dec-Apr  + Jun-Sep whale-shark event peak","commission":"local dive-op → OTA affiliate"},{"name":"Punta Sur loggerhead-turtle dive","si_tag":"diveglobal","status":"future","tier":"premier","hook":"summer mating aggregation in south-point current","bookable_category":"guided drift dive","source":"https://www.pocnadivecenter.com/post/scuba-diving-with-loggerheads-in-isla-mujeres","si":"diveglobal","blurb":"summer mating aggregation in south-point current","commission":"local dive-op (advanced) → curated-recommend"},{"name":"Playa Norte at dawn","si_tag":"tropical","status":"live","tier":"comfort","hook":"waist-deep glass-calm turquoise, sargassum-protected","bookable_category":"hotel + ferry","source":"https://www.howisthesargassum.com/blog/cancun-hurricane-season-2026","timing":"Dec-Apr  + Jun-Sep whale-shark event peak","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"tropical","blurb":"waist-deep glass-calm turquoise, sargassum-protected","when":"Dec-Apr  + Jun-Sep whale-shark event peak","commission":"bed-bank/boutique portal → OTA; ferry pass-through"},{"name":"Isla Contoy day trip","si_tag":"globaladv","status":"future","tier":"comfort","hook":"200/day capped bird-sanctuary reserve + Ixlaché reef","bookable_category":"authorized eco day tour","source":"https://contoyadventures.com/isla-contoy/","timing":"Dec-Apr  + Jun-Sep whale-shark event peak","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"adventure","blurb":"200/day capped bird-sanctuary reserve + Ixlaché reef","when":"Dec-Apr  + Jun-Sep whale-shark event peak","commission":"authorized Contoy operator/DMC → curated (fee pass-through)"}],"faq":[{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for on Isla Mujeres?","a":"Water, weather and currents — not crime. Drink bottled water, use repellent for dengue (no malaria in the tourist zone), and note hurricane season runs June–November with September riskiest. Playa Norte is comparatively sargassum-protected, but 2026 is heavy region-wide; the Punta Sur loggerhead dives sit in strong currents, so they are for advanced divers only.","source":"howisthesargassum.com","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Is swimming with whale sharks or diving Punta Sur dangerous?","a":"The whale-shark encounter is snorkel-only with no decompression restriction — wear the vest, no touching, stay with the guide against boat traffic and open-water current. Punta Sur''s summer loggerhead dive is a strong-current drift for advanced divers with a local guide; observe no-fly of 18–24 hours after any scuba.","source":"pocnadivecenter.com","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"When and how can I swim with whale sharks from Isla Mujeres?","a":"Roughly June to September, on a snorkel-only boat excursion to the aggregation — the island is the whale-shark snorkel capital of the region. Tours book about 30–39 days out on average and sell out fast in peak summer, so reserve at least 3–6 weeks ahead; it is snorkel-only, with no scuba allowed.","source":"mexicodivers.com","si_tag":"ocean"},{"q":"Can beginners dive MUSA from Isla Mujeres?","a":"Yes — MUSA is one of the most accessible dives anywhere. Its 470+ statues sit just 3.5–8 m down, shallow enough for Open Water divers and snorkelers, and at ≤9 m these are easy day dives. Advanced divers can add the Punta Sur loggerhead drift in summer, which sits in strong current and is guided-only.","source":"bluewaterdivetravel.com","si_tag":"diveglobal"},{"q":"Is Playa Norte good, and will sargassum ruin it?","a":"It is the island''s signature beach — waist-deep, glass-calm turquoise you can wade out a hundred meters into — and one of the most sargassum-protected stretches in the region. In a heavy year like 2026 that protection is a genuine edge, but still disclose: no beach is fully immune, and mornings are cleanest.","source":"howisthesargassum.com","si_tag":"tropical"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Isla Mujeres, Mexico: Whale Sharks, MUSA & Playa Norte","meta_description":"A golf-cart island off Cancún — snorkel the whale-shark run, dive MUSA and Punta Sur loggerheads, and wade Playa Norte''s calm turquoise. Season, safety, booking.","slug":"isla-mujeres-mexico","primary_keyword":"Isla Mujeres whale shark snorkeling","long_tail":["Isla Mujeres MUSA diving","Playa Norte Isla Mujeres","Punta Sur loggerhead turtles","Isla Mujeres whale shark season","Isla Contoy tour from Isla Mujeres"],"search_language":"es-MX (restated, not machine-translated)","local_keywords":["nadar con tiburón ballena Isla Mujeres","buceo MUSA Cancún","Playa Norte Isla Mujeres","temporada de tiburón ballena","tortugas caguama Punta Sur","qué hacer en Isla Mujeres","villas de lujo Isla Mujeres"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","content_freshness":"2026-07-04"},"booking":{"bin":"freely_bookable","level":"L2","codes":[],"consent_flow":false,"note":"Quintana Roo/Mexico US L2 (Exercise Increased Caution) - freely bookable; MXN currency, USD widely accepted"},"si_checklist_25":{"run_date":"2026-07-31","hits":7,"misses":15,"disregarded":3,"note":"Canonical 25-SI list; sports limited to participant; spectator/prosports/compsports disregarded"},"sis_present":[{"si":"tropical","name":"tropical","status":"live"},{"si":"ocean","name":"ocean","status":"future"},{"si":"diveglobal","name":"diveglobal","status":"future"},{"si":"globaladv","name":"adventure","status":"future"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Impression Isla Mujeres by Secrets","why_ultra":"125 all-suite adults-only, butler + Endless Privileges, 8 restaurants, private catamaran transfer; ''Most Instagrammable Hotel in the World'' 2 yrs running — island''s true ultra flagship","earning":"on application / via host-Virtuoso (Hyatt Inclusive Collection); verify %","virtuoso_value_add":"verify Virtuoso/Hyatt Prive amenities - not documented","mor":"commission-on-net; no net-rate resale markup","source":"https://www.hyattinclusivecollection.com/en/resorts-hotels/impression-by-secrets/mexico/isla-mujeres/"},{"name":"Mia Reef Isla Mujeres (All-Inclusive)","why_ultra":"private-island feel at Playa Norte tip, dock-connected, 93 rooms + 63 suites, King''s Pool snorkel lagoon — upper-luxe marquee, not five-diamond (reviews flag dated facilities)","earning":"on application via host/OTA; verify","virtuoso_value_add":"verify - not documented","mor":"commission-on-net; no resale markup","source":"https://www.tripadvisor.com/Hotel_Review-g150810-d259074-Reviews-Mia_Reef_Isla_Mujeres-Isla_Mujeres_Yucatan_Peninsula.html"},{"name":"Nearest true ultra: Cancún Nizuc / Playa Mujeres / Mayakoba corridor (mainland)","why_ultra":"AAA Five-Diamond / Virtuoso-preferred ultra is mainland (Nizuc, Mayakoba Rosewood/Banyan Tree/Fairmont/Andaz); Isla Mujeres = day-trip / honeymoon-island add-on","earning":"on application - see Puerto Morelos/Mayakoba dossier","virtuoso_value_add":"see corridor dossier","mor":"commission-on-net","source":"https://www.jetsetchristina.com/where-to-stay-in-mayakoba-mexico-rosewood-vs-fairmont-vs-andaz-vs-banyan-tree/"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-04","hero":{"query":"Isla Mujeres, Mexico"},"geo":{"lat":21.2311,"lng":-86.7311}}'::jsonb, 51),
  ('izamal-mexico', '10S', 'Izamal', 'Mexico', 'A whole city painted the color of afternoon light', 'live', 'verified', 'kyoto', 'Yucatán (Mérida & Chichén Itzá)', '{"culture","romance","culinary"}', '{}', '{"comfort","premier","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["Mexico''s FIRST Pueblo Mágico, designated 2002-02-16 — launched the entire Magical Towns program","Convento de San Antonio de Padua founded 1549 / completed 1561 atop a Maya temple; 75-arch atrium among the largest monastery atriums in the world","Kinich Kakmó pyramid ~200m x ~180m, c. 400-600 AD, dedicated to the Maya sun god, climbable to the summit","Pope John Paul II visited August 1993; standardized ochre-yellow color tradition dates to that visit (''the Yellow City'')","~70 km / ~1h10 from Mérida — an easy day-trip, roughly midway toward Chichén Itzá"],"safety":{"emergency_number":"911","nearest_trauma":"Mérida (~1h10 west; regional hospital hub)","advisory_level":"L1","book_enabled":true,"air_access_verified":true,"air_access_note":"MID Mérida ~1h10 drive; US nonstops incl. Houston, Miami, Dallas, Atlanta","primary_hazards":["heat/sun exposure (shadeless plazas + exposed pyramid climb)","Kinich Kakmó footing (steep, handrail-free Maya steps)","calesa/town traffic (low)","dengue (rainy season)","non-potable tap water"],"climbing_note":"Kinich Kakmó IS climbable to summit — genuine draw; steep uneven risers, no handrails","fcdo":{"posture":"AREA-RESTRICTED","quotes":[{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel State of Baja California FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tijuana, except: airside transit through Tijuana airport the Cross Border Xpress bridge from the airport linking terminals across the Mexican-US border the federal toll road 1D and Via Rápida through Tijuana to the border FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tecate in Baja California, including roads between Tijuana and Tecate."},{"form":